WEBVTT

00:00:06.098 --> 00:00:08.100 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:35.002 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:39.631 line:80%
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:41.008 line:80%
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:00:41.675 --> 00:00:42.885 line:80%
[high-pitched ringing]

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:44.470 line:80%
[♪ surreal music playing]

00:00:47.473 --> 00:00:48.474 line:80%
[explosion]

00:00:53.771 --> 00:00:54.772 line:80%
[Haran] What is it?

00:00:56.815 --> 00:00:57.858 line:80%
Are you okay?

00:01:01.487 --> 00:01:02.488 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:01:02.571 --> 00:01:05.032 line:80%
Yes, it was just the lights.

00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:06.367 line:80%
I'm fine.

00:01:07.493 --> 00:01:10.079 line:80%
No, you don't look fine.

00:01:11.497 --> 00:01:12.498 line:80%
I am.

00:01:12.581 --> 00:01:17.294 line:80%
I won't cause you any trouble,
especially during the three-month trial.

00:01:17.586 --> 00:01:18.587 line:80%
[sighs]

00:01:20.339 --> 00:01:21.340 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:01:22.758 --> 00:01:24.301 line:80%
[Chan] <i>It was my first time</i>
<i>hearing that sound.</i>

00:01:24.385 --> 00:01:25.969 line:80%
[♪ pensive music playing]

00:01:26.053 --> 00:01:30.474 line:20%
<i>It kind of sounded like tiny bits</i>
<i>of metal clinking or ice rattling.</i>

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.725 line:80%
<i>Right, the door!</i>

00:01:31.809 --> 00:01:34.311 line:80%
<i>I think it came from outside the lab.</i>

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:36.480 line:20%
EPISODE 4

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.773 line:20%
But I'm not sure what that sound was

00:01:37.856 --> 00:01:40.109 line:20%
or why I was suddenly reminded
of the explosion.

00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:41.652 line:20%
[doctor breathes deeply]

00:01:41.735 --> 00:01:43.487 line:20%
From everything I've heard so far,

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.699 line:20%
it's most likely
that it's a second trigger.

00:01:47.366 --> 00:01:49.034 line:20%
A second trigger?

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:51.412 line:20%
<i>It's nice to meet you.</i>

00:01:51.495 --> 00:01:53.163 line:20%
I'm Song Haran, the lead designer.

00:01:53.247 --> 00:01:57.001 line:20%
[doctor] <i>It seems that</i>
<i>seeing her again acted as a trigger.</i>

00:01:57.084 --> 00:02:00.045 line:20%
She seems to have stimulated something,

00:02:00.129 --> 00:02:02.297 line:80%
allowing you to remember
another piece of your past.

00:02:02.381 --> 00:02:04.967 line:80%
[chuckles] Wait. No…

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.678 line:80%
[stutters] That doesn't make any sense.

00:02:07.761 --> 00:02:09.805 line:80%
I recalled everything seven years ago.

00:02:09.888 --> 00:02:13.809 line:80%
When I first saw her at Jamsugyo,
I remembered everything in Boston.

00:02:13.892 --> 00:02:16.145 line:80%
How are you sure it was everything?

00:02:16.228 --> 00:02:19.565 line:80%
Well, because it was only
a temporary side effect

00:02:19.648 --> 00:02:22.693 line:80%
from the shock of the accident.

00:02:22.776 --> 00:02:27.031 line:80%
You're saying you remembered
everything at that moment?

00:02:27.114 --> 00:02:31.577 line:80%
Yes. And I've never recalled
any new sounds or images since then.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:32.911 line:80%
Not once.

00:02:32.995 --> 00:02:34.288 line:80%
What if…

00:02:35.664 --> 00:02:37.666 line:80%
-Like this…
-[eraser scraping]

00:02:39.418 --> 00:02:43.505 line:80%
What if there is still an empty spot
in your memories that you're not aware of?

00:02:44.423 --> 00:02:46.675 line:80%
An empty spot?

00:02:47.259 --> 00:02:50.137 line:80%
[doctor] You seem like
a completely different person now.

00:02:50.721 --> 00:02:54.642 line:80%
<i>I can even picture</i>
<i>how hard you tried to change yourself.</i>

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:01.565 line:80%
<i>The harder you try to shake off the past,</i>
<i>the more your defense mechanisms kick in.</i>

00:03:01.649 --> 00:03:04.318 line:80%
<i>Your unconscious mind</i>
<i>may overwrite painful memories</i>

00:03:04.401 --> 00:03:07.613 line:80%
<i>to keep you from suffering any longer.</i>

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:14.286 line:80%
<i>It means there's still</i>
<i>an empty spot inside you.</i>

00:03:16.789 --> 00:03:20.959 line:80%
[Chan] <i>If that sound</i>
<i>is a part of that empty spot,</i>

00:03:21.043 --> 00:03:23.253 line:80%
<i>is it a signal from the past</i>

00:03:24.922 --> 00:03:28.300 line:80%
<i>telling me it's linked</i>
<i>to the explosion seven years ago?</i>

00:03:31.637 --> 00:03:34.348 line:80%
[doctor] <i>We can't be sure</i>
<i>of anything right now, but…</i>

00:03:35.015 --> 00:03:36.600 line:80%
<i>it's certain that</i>

00:03:36.684 --> 00:03:39.853 line:80%
<i>she's the one who has the key</i>
<i>to that empty spot inside you.</i>

00:03:39.937 --> 00:03:41.897 line:80%
-[water gushing]
-[♪ music fades]

00:03:41.981 --> 00:03:43.983 line:80%
You don't seem happy to see me.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.903 line:80%
I mustered up my courage
to come and celebrate starting the trial.

00:03:52.157 --> 00:03:53.367 line:80%
That's cold!

00:03:53.909 --> 00:03:58.372 line:80%
Mmm. I always give a water show
to people I'm excited to see.

00:03:59.331 --> 00:04:01.291 line:80%
-[scoffs]
-[Chan chuckles]

00:04:01.375 --> 00:04:03.043 line:80%
Hey, look who it is!

00:04:03.627 --> 00:04:04.920 line:80%
[exclaims] How have you been, Genius?

00:04:05.004 --> 00:04:06.171 line:80%
-[Genius barks]
-[Haran chuckles]

00:04:06.255 --> 00:04:09.717 line:80%
-[Haran] How are you?
-It's been such a long time.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.301 line:80%
What are you doing here so early?

00:04:11.385 --> 00:04:13.303 line:80%
I wanted to have your coffee.

00:04:13.387 --> 00:04:15.264 line:80%
I'm aching
from not having any for so long.

00:04:15.347 --> 00:04:17.433 line:80%
Really? Then I should make you some now.

00:04:17.516 --> 00:04:18.559 line:80%
Come on in.

00:04:18.642 --> 00:04:20.686 line:80%
-Let's go, Genius.
-[Manjae] Come inside.

00:04:23.022 --> 00:04:26.108 line:80%
[doctor] <i>If you don't want to suffer again</i>
<i>because of your past,</i>

00:04:26.191 --> 00:04:28.610 line:80%
<i>it would be best</i>
<i>to keep a distance from her.</i>

00:04:28.694 --> 00:04:30.738 line:80%
To protect yourself,

00:04:30.821 --> 00:04:34.033 line:80%
a lock is safer than a key at the moment.

00:04:34.783 --> 00:04:36.660 line:80%
[whispers] A lock…

00:04:38.912 --> 00:04:40.914 line:80%
-[♪ heartwarming music playing]
-[sighs]

00:04:42.791 --> 00:04:44.418 line:80%
-[coffee pouring]
-[door opens]

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.712 line:80%
-Sit down, roomie.
-Okay.

00:04:46.795 --> 00:04:49.548 line:80%
Here's some coffee for my VVIP.

00:04:49.631 --> 00:04:51.342 line:80%
Thank you. [inhales sharply]

00:04:51.717 --> 00:04:52.718 line:80%
[Chan] Huh?

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:56.180 line:80%
Right. It must have recovered
from the transplant shock.

00:04:56.972 --> 00:05:00.184 line:80%
[sighs contentedly]
Good thing I repotted it, right?

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:01.435 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:05:01.518 --> 00:05:03.604 line:80%
-Yes.
-[Manjae] Right. [chuckles]

00:05:04.438 --> 00:05:06.023 line:80%
It's a good thing you took it out.

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.695 line:80%
<i>Even if I break down again,</i>
<i>I'll stay by her side.</i>

00:05:11.779 --> 00:05:12.780 line:80%
Mmm.

00:05:12.863 --> 00:05:16.075 line:80%
[Chan] <i>She's the one</i>
<i>who gave me the life I have now.</i>

00:05:16.158 --> 00:05:19.828 line:80%
<i>I would have died</i>
<i>if it hadn't been for her.</i>

00:05:22.373 --> 00:05:23.499 line:80%
Why are you staring at me?

00:05:24.333 --> 00:05:26.335 line:80%
Mmm… Can't I look at you?

00:05:27.127 --> 00:05:29.213 line:80%
Here. Cheers. [grunts]

00:05:35.469 --> 00:05:37.971 line:80%
[Haran slurps, sighs contentedly]

00:05:38.722 --> 00:05:40.474 line:80%
<i>Whatever's hiding in that empty spot,</i>

00:05:41.433 --> 00:05:42.851 line:80%
I'm going to deal with it.

00:05:43.602 --> 00:05:47.398 line:80%
As long as she becomes happy,
I don't care what happens.

00:05:48.607 --> 00:05:49.984 line:80%
<i>I'll be careful</i>

00:05:50.693 --> 00:05:53.988 line:80%
<i>so my existence doesn't reopen</i>
<i>her old wounds…</i>

00:05:55.656 --> 00:05:58.158 line:80%
and I'll do everything I can for her
before I leave again.

00:06:05.749 --> 00:06:07.668 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:06:08.877 --> 00:06:09.878 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:06:09.962 --> 00:06:11.213 line:80%
Did you check the data?

00:06:11.296 --> 00:06:12.464 line:80%
Yes.

00:06:12.548 --> 00:06:15.509 line:20%
The background team's research
was a little lacking.

00:06:15.592 --> 00:06:17.094 line:80%
When did you organize all this?

00:06:17.177 --> 00:06:21.432 line:80%
There was a lot of modernized material,
so I researched traditional <i>hanok.</i>

00:06:21.515 --> 00:06:25.477 line:80%
I guess a Korean
should have researched traditional <i>hanok.</i>

00:06:25.561 --> 00:06:26.562 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:06:26.645 --> 00:06:29.189 line:80%
[in English] Okay,
I'll send this over to the EA team,

00:06:29.273 --> 00:06:32.484 line:80%
and we can go down to Gyeongju on Tuesday.

00:06:32.568 --> 00:06:34.320 line:80%
[in Korean] Oh. I'll join you a day late.

00:06:34.403 --> 00:06:37.823 line:80%
Ms. Kim said she'll send over
the <i>dancheong </i>design draft on Tuesday.

00:06:37.906 --> 00:06:38.907 line:80%
[Ben in English] Mmm. Okay.

00:06:39.867 --> 00:06:42.119 line:80%
[in Korean]
But how will you get there, then?

00:06:42.202 --> 00:06:45.456 line:80%
-I'll rent a car.
-Are you sure?

00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:48.584 line:80%
I'll be absolutely fine.

00:06:49.168 --> 00:06:50.169 line:80%
[chuckles nervously]

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.049 line:80%
Hey, stop writing that.

00:06:55.132 --> 00:06:56.467 line:80%
Fine.

00:06:57.051 --> 00:06:59.094 line:80%
-Geez!
-[Chan] We'd like to pay.

00:06:59.178 --> 00:07:00.179 line:80%
BEN IS AN IDIOT

00:07:01.347 --> 00:07:03.015 line:80%
Ms. Song!

00:07:03.098 --> 00:07:05.434 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:07:05.517 --> 00:07:06.935 line:80%
What is he doing?

00:07:08.479 --> 00:07:09.563 line:80%
You're done with work, right?

00:07:10.564 --> 00:07:11.899 line:80%
Are you busy, by any chance?

00:07:12.358 --> 00:07:13.400 line:80%
[in English] Nice!

00:07:14.777 --> 00:07:16.904 line:80%
[in Korean] Then get in.

00:07:16.987 --> 00:07:20.866 line:80%
-What? Where are we going?
-There's a car coming.

00:07:20.949 --> 00:07:25.954 line:80%
I have a special lecture tomorrow,
so wrap up the contract with our buyer.

00:07:26.038 --> 00:07:27.665 line:80%
-Yes, ma'am.
-Get in. Come on.

00:07:28.707 --> 00:07:30.542 line:80%
-[Chan] Watch your head.
-[car honks]

00:07:30.626 --> 00:07:31.627 line:80%
Sorry!

00:07:32.961 --> 00:07:34.004 line:80%
[in English] Oh, yeah.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:38.592 line:80%
[in Korean] Did you just say, "Oh, yeah"?

00:07:38.676 --> 00:07:39.677 line:80%
Those two.

00:07:40.552 --> 00:07:41.637 line:80%
Keep an eye on them.

00:07:42.096 --> 00:07:43.097 line:80%
Bye, then.

00:07:47.017 --> 00:07:48.769 line:80%
So they weren't lying to me.

00:07:50.229 --> 00:07:51.230 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:07:52.356 --> 00:07:54.441 line:80%
We came all the way here for chicken?

00:07:54.525 --> 00:07:56.735 line:80%
This is a must in Korea.

00:07:56.819 --> 00:07:59.196 line:80%
Hangang River, picnic mat, and chicken.

00:07:59.947 --> 00:08:02.449 line:80%
I'm also a tourist from abroad, you know.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:05.869 line:80%
Wow!

00:08:05.953 --> 00:08:08.038 line:80%
The Hangang River is so nice.

00:08:08.122 --> 00:08:10.499 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:08:15.587 --> 00:08:16.964 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:08:17.047 --> 00:08:18.924 line:80%
I have something to give you. Sit down.

00:08:21.885 --> 00:08:24.513 line:80%
There are 0.3, 0.4, 5, 6,

00:08:24.596 --> 00:08:27.266 line:80%
oil-based, water-based,
nib tip, and ballpoint pens.

00:08:27.349 --> 00:08:29.977 line:80%
Wait. Are you opening a stationery store?

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:32.313 line:80%
Who has this many pens?

00:08:32.396 --> 00:08:35.566 line:80%
I have a habit of buying new pens
for people who lose their pens.

00:08:36.942 --> 00:08:38.944 line:80%
-[sighs softly]
-[Chan sighs]

00:08:39.028 --> 00:08:41.655 line:80%
There should at least be
one pen that you like.

00:08:47.411 --> 00:08:50.372 line:80%
But the trial hasn't started yet.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.292 line:80%
This is like a preview.

00:08:53.375 --> 00:08:54.543 line:80%
A preview of what?

00:08:54.626 --> 00:08:57.963 line:80%
I'll be away for about two weeks
starting Wednesday

00:08:58.047 --> 00:08:59.089 line:80%
for a field survey.

00:08:59.923 --> 00:09:01.467 line:80%
I said we'd get close,

00:09:02.134 --> 00:09:04.678 line:80%
but if I left without doing anything,
nothing would change.

00:09:04.762 --> 00:09:05.888 line:80%
And I didn't want that.

00:09:07.306 --> 00:09:08.974 line:80%
So…

00:09:09.058 --> 00:09:10.059 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:09:10.142 --> 00:09:11.268 line:80%
will you take this, too?

00:09:13.312 --> 00:09:14.313 line:80%
Oh…

00:09:15.064 --> 00:09:16.815 line:80%
SEOUL DESTINATIONS LIST

00:09:16.899 --> 00:09:18.651 line:80%
Why are you giving this to me?

00:09:18.734 --> 00:09:21.779 line:80%
Choose where to go first
so we can go together later.

00:09:21.862 --> 00:09:22.863 line:80%
[cell phone buzzes]

00:09:24.198 --> 00:09:26.492 line:80%
[exclaims] The chicken's here.
I'll go get it.

00:09:27.326 --> 00:09:28.952 line:80%
[grunts] Can you clean that up?

00:09:30.079 --> 00:09:33.332 line:80%
Oh. It's this way.
We have to eat chicken here, so hurry!

00:09:40.464 --> 00:09:41.674 line:80%
"That person"?

00:09:44.635 --> 00:09:46.595 line:80%
[exclaims excitedly]
The night view is beautiful.

00:09:46.679 --> 00:09:47.680 line:80%
-Right?
-[camera clicks]

00:09:47.763 --> 00:09:50.766 line:80%
How about going to Jamsugyo on Christmas?
It's the best spot

00:09:50.849 --> 00:09:52.685 line:80%
-to watch the fireworks.
-[woman gasps]

00:09:52.768 --> 00:09:54.561 line:80%
-[woman] I'd love that. [giggles]
-Jamsugyo?

00:09:55.854 --> 00:09:56.939 line:80%
[couple] Cheers.

00:09:59.733 --> 00:10:01.986 line:80%
[♪ "Jingle Bell" playing over speakers]

00:10:06.782 --> 00:10:08.158 line:80%
[taxi driver] Goodness.

00:10:08.242 --> 00:10:09.660 line:80%
We're really stuck.

00:10:09.743 --> 00:10:12.371 line:80%
I heard they're showing fireworks
at 7:00. [sighs]

00:10:12.454 --> 00:10:14.039 line:80%
We're not moving at all.

00:10:15.749 --> 00:10:16.917 line:80%
[sighs]

00:10:17.001 --> 00:10:20.004 line:80%
How long will it take?
I have an important meeting.

00:10:20.087 --> 00:10:23.257 line:80%
If it's urgent, it would be faster
to just walk across the bridge.

00:10:26.635 --> 00:10:27.803 line:80%
Mr. Yoon.

00:10:27.886 --> 00:10:29.805 line:80%
The traffic's bad
since it's Christmas Eve.

00:10:31.098 --> 00:10:32.599 line:80%
Really?

00:10:32.683 --> 00:10:34.560 line:80%
Then take your time.

00:10:34.643 --> 00:10:35.936 line:80%
All right.

00:10:36.478 --> 00:10:37.479 line:80%
[call disconnects]

00:10:37.563 --> 00:10:41.150 line:80%
[♪ J.S. Bach "Goldberg Variations,
BWV 988: Aria" playing over speakers]

00:11:03.756 --> 00:11:05.674 line:80%
[firework whistles, pops]

00:11:05.758 --> 00:11:07.926 line:80%
[people exclaiming]

00:11:17.144 --> 00:11:20.189 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Hey, Kang Hyeokchan.</i>
<i>Why aren't you picking up?</i>

00:11:20.272 --> 00:11:22.691 line:80%
[Hyeokchan] <i>Sorry, I fell asleep.</i>

00:11:23.651 --> 00:11:24.902 line:80%
<i>Maybe I have insomnia.</i>

00:11:24.985 --> 00:11:28.489 line:80%
<i>My sleep pattern is messed up,</i>
<i>so I'm sleeping at random times.</i>

00:11:28.572 --> 00:11:31.367 line:80%
[Haran] <i>They said it helps with insomnia.</i>

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.661 line:80%
<i>Try listening to it</i>
<i>when you can't sleep. Okay?</i>

00:11:35.579 --> 00:11:36.580 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:11:40.709 --> 00:11:42.086 line:80%
Let's go.

00:11:42.169 --> 00:11:43.796 line:80%
-What? Right now?
-Yes.

00:11:43.879 --> 00:11:45.297 line:80%
[man 1] Should we order fried chicken?

00:11:45.381 --> 00:11:47.216 line:80%
-Isn't seasoned chicken better?
-Hang on.

00:11:47.299 --> 00:11:48.717 line:80%
[man 2] No, fried is better.

00:11:48.801 --> 00:11:50.928 line:80%
-Here you go!
-[man 1] What's this?

00:11:51.011 --> 00:11:52.429 line:80%
You won some free chicken.

00:11:52.513 --> 00:11:54.598 line:80%
-We can have this? Wow.
-Of course.

00:11:54.682 --> 00:11:56.308 line:80%
[Chan] It's still warm, so enjoy.

00:11:56.392 --> 00:11:58.143 line:80%
[men] Thank you.

00:11:58.227 --> 00:11:59.436 line:80%
[Chan grunts]

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.398 line:80%
Come on. These are valuable,
so don't forget them.

00:12:02.481 --> 00:12:04.400 line:80%
-[♪ amusing music playing]
-[Chan groans]

00:12:04.483 --> 00:12:06.610 line:80%
Chicken was too predictable, right?

00:12:07.277 --> 00:12:09.738 line:80%
Let's go with charcoal-grilled meat.

00:12:09.822 --> 00:12:11.407 line:80%
-Ben recommended--
-[♪ music fades]

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.784 line:80%
[stammers] All right, fine.

00:12:14.576 --> 00:12:15.619 line:80%
But what's with these?

00:12:15.703 --> 00:12:17.204 line:80%
-[bike bell chimes]
-Ah.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:21.250 line:80%
We're going to cross Jamsugyo with these.
It's the fastest way.

00:12:22.334 --> 00:12:26.547 line:80%
I'm sorry, but I'd like to just go now.

00:12:27.506 --> 00:12:28.924 line:80%
[exclaims teasingly]

00:12:29.758 --> 00:12:31.260 line:80%
No way.

00:12:31.343 --> 00:12:33.053 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Can you not ride a bike?

00:12:33.137 --> 00:12:34.722 line:80%
No, it's not that…

00:12:34.805 --> 00:12:36.724 line:80%
-No, it's okay.
-[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:12:36.807 --> 00:12:39.101 line:80%
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:12:39.643 --> 00:12:41.645 line:80%
-I'll return them.
-No, I…

00:12:41.729 --> 00:12:43.981 line:80%
I know how to ride a bike, but…

00:12:46.567 --> 00:12:48.694 line:80%
Fine. Let's go, then.

00:12:48.777 --> 00:12:49.778 line:80%
[in English] Okay!

00:12:50.487 --> 00:12:51.572 line:80%
[in Korean] All right.

00:12:52.197 --> 00:12:54.616 line:80%
Since it's boring to just ride there,
how about a bet?

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.244 line:80%
-The last one there buys dinner. Okay?
-[♪ music fades]

00:12:57.328 --> 00:12:58.871 line:80%
No, there's no need…

00:12:58.954 --> 00:13:00.039 line:80%
-Let's just--
-Ready, go!

00:13:01.915 --> 00:13:04.084 line:80%
That's cheating.

00:13:04.168 --> 00:13:06.170 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming song playing]

00:13:10.215 --> 00:13:11.216 line:80%
Oh…

00:13:12.009 --> 00:13:13.802 line:80%
Whoa. Wait…

00:13:13.886 --> 00:13:15.971 line:80%
Hang on! My leg…

00:13:16.055 --> 00:13:17.514 line:80%
Wait, wait!

00:13:17.598 --> 00:13:19.391 line:80%
What is it? What's wrong with your leg?

00:13:21.644 --> 00:13:22.645 line:80%
It's long.

00:13:23.187 --> 00:13:24.188 line:80%
What?

00:13:24.271 --> 00:13:25.689 line:80%
-[chuckles]
-Ah…

00:13:25.773 --> 00:13:27.608 line:80%
[stutters] Geez.

00:13:29.318 --> 00:13:30.778 line:80%
[exclaims]

00:13:32.154 --> 00:13:34.156 line:80%
-[Haran exclaims excitedly]
-[chuckling]

00:13:34.948 --> 00:13:35.949 line:80%
[yells excitedly]

00:13:38.494 --> 00:13:39.495 line:80%
[Haran] Wow!

00:13:40.871 --> 00:13:41.872 line:80%
Wow.

00:13:45.459 --> 00:13:46.460 line:80%
Whoa.

00:13:47.419 --> 00:13:49.463 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming song continuing]

00:14:17.241 --> 00:14:20.577 line:80%
[Chan] Wow, it's beautiful.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.121 line:80%
Isn't it?

00:14:30.504 --> 00:14:32.965 line:80%
-Wow. The Hangang River is nice.
-[♪ song fades]

00:14:33.549 --> 00:14:35.843 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Were you mimicking me?

00:14:35.926 --> 00:14:38.554 line:80%
But that's not how you do it.

00:14:38.637 --> 00:14:41.932 line:80%
Wow!

00:14:42.016 --> 00:14:44.184 line:80%
Hangang River is really nice.

00:14:44.268 --> 00:14:45.269 line:80%
What's the difference?

00:14:45.352 --> 00:14:46.729 line:80%
-It sounds the same.
-It's different.

00:14:46.812 --> 00:14:47.896 line:80%
[scoffs]

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:49.565 line:80%
I won, so you're buying.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:53.402 line:80%
We haven't even gotten there yet.

00:14:54.987 --> 00:14:56.488 line:80%
[Haran yells excitedly]

00:15:00.159 --> 00:15:02.411 line:80%
[Hayeong in English] Good morning.

00:15:03.954 --> 00:15:05.414 line:80%
[chuckles] Ah!

00:15:05.497 --> 00:15:07.583 line:80%
-[in Korean] Hi, Hadam.
-[in English] Good morning.

00:15:09.043 --> 00:15:10.836 line:80%
[in Korean] You know
Yougyum's coming today, right?

00:15:10.919 --> 00:15:12.713 line:80%
He's coming at 7:00 p.m.,
so don't be late.

00:15:12.796 --> 00:15:15.716 line:80%
Of course. We've been waiting
impatiently for this day.

00:15:15.799 --> 00:15:18.761 line:80%
We'll have you rascals
sit down in front of us

00:15:18.844 --> 00:15:21.388 line:80%
while we look him over from head to toe…

00:15:21.472 --> 00:15:24.266 line:80%
Hey! I'm not done talking.

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:25.851 line:80%
You did go on for quite a bit.

00:15:26.727 --> 00:15:27.936 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:31.690 line:80%
Haran, she can't be serious
about getting married, can she?

00:15:31.774 --> 00:15:34.943 line:80%
I don't know. We'll see.

00:15:37.154 --> 00:15:38.155 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:15:38.238 --> 00:15:41.367 line:80%
CHEONGSOL BASEBALL TEAM CHA YOUGYUM
IS JOINING THE MAJOR LEAGUE

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:43.369 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:15:45.621 --> 00:15:46.914 line:80%
No way. It's Han Sora.

00:15:46.997 --> 00:15:48.082 line:80%
She came to school today?

00:15:48.916 --> 00:15:51.251 line:80%
[Yougyum] What? Who are you?

00:15:51.335 --> 00:15:52.670 line:80%
Why do you want my number?

00:15:52.753 --> 00:15:53.754 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:15:53.837 --> 00:15:57.508 line:80%
Because I'm interested in you, of course.

00:15:57.591 --> 00:15:59.093 line:80%
[students exclaim]

00:15:59.176 --> 00:16:01.095 line:80%
I'm not interested in you at all.

00:16:01.178 --> 00:16:02.554 line:80%
And I have a girlfriend.

00:16:02.638 --> 00:16:03.973 line:80%
[Hadam] Yougyum.

00:16:04.056 --> 00:16:05.140 line:80%
Hey, Hadam.

00:16:06.141 --> 00:16:07.351 line:80%
[Yougyum chuckles]

00:16:08.769 --> 00:16:09.770 line:80%
What's going on?

00:16:09.853 --> 00:16:11.146 line:80%
It's nothing.

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:14.024 line:80%
Ah. Is she your girlfriend?

00:16:15.526 --> 00:16:16.944 line:80%
[scoffs] I'll see you later.

00:16:22.741 --> 00:16:24.660 line:80%
Who is she? Do you know her?

00:16:25.285 --> 00:16:28.455 line:80%
Not at all.
It's the last time I'll even speak to her.

00:16:28.539 --> 00:16:30.165 line:80%
Hey, don't you know? It's her.

00:16:30.249 --> 00:16:32.376 line:80%
-Han Sora, the girl group trainee--
-Hadam!

00:16:32.459 --> 00:16:34.753 line:80%
Have a good day. I'll see you later.

00:16:34.837 --> 00:16:36.588 line:80%
-[chuckles awkwardly]
-[♪ amusing music playing]

00:16:36.672 --> 00:16:38.716 line:80%
-She must really like you.
-[Yougyum] Be quiet, will you?

00:16:38.799 --> 00:16:40.092 line:80%
Come on!

00:16:40.175 --> 00:16:42.011 line:80%
-[player 1] She's so pretty, though.
-[player 2] Right?

00:16:42.094 --> 00:16:43.220 line:80%
[Yougyum] Shut up, you guys.

00:16:43.303 --> 00:16:44.680 line:80%
[Changmo] She has her eyes set on you.
You should date her.

00:16:45.222 --> 00:16:46.724 line:80%
[Yougyum] Be quiet. Shut up.

00:16:46.807 --> 00:16:48.809 line:80%
[player 3] That's the problem
with handsome guys.

00:16:49.685 --> 00:16:50.811 line:80%
"Han Sora"?

00:16:53.314 --> 00:16:54.315 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:16:58.152 --> 00:16:59.361 line:80%
[pens rattle]

00:17:03.324 --> 00:17:04.325 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:07.995 line:80%
[pen scraping]

00:17:09.538 --> 00:17:10.831 line:80%
Hmm? [exclaims]

00:17:12.166 --> 00:17:13.167 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:17:19.089 --> 00:17:21.091 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[phone ringing]

00:17:24.553 --> 00:17:26.472 line:80%
This is Design Team 1 of Nana Atelier--

00:17:26.555 --> 00:17:28.140 line:80%
[Nana] <i>Why isn't anyone picking up?</i>

00:17:30.768 --> 00:17:31.935 line:80%
Why are you calling here?

00:17:32.019 --> 00:17:33.729 line:80%
This is urgent. Listen carefully.

00:17:33.854 --> 00:17:36.690 line:80%
<i>It's a womenswear lecture,</i>
<i>but I brought menswear materials.</i>

00:17:36.815 --> 00:17:40.110 line:80%
<i>-That's on me. We don't have much time.</i>
-Taxi! Taxi! Over here!

00:17:40.194 --> 00:17:42.321 line:80%
[Nana] <i>I need you here in 30 minutes.</i>

00:17:42.404 --> 00:17:44.907 line:80%
-[Haran gasping] What do I do?
-[car honks]

00:17:48.452 --> 00:17:49.495 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:17:49.578 --> 00:17:52.164 line:80%
-Hey, my neighbor!
-Oh… Do you have some time?

00:17:52.247 --> 00:17:54.124 line:80%
Sure, I'm totally free.

00:17:54.208 --> 00:17:55.834 line:80%
I rented this car, so I'm taking a drive--

00:17:55.918 --> 00:17:57.753 line:80%
[sighs in relief] That's great! Then…

00:17:57.836 --> 00:17:59.755 line:80%
Then can you…

00:17:59.838 --> 00:18:02.174 line:80%
I have an urgent meeting,
but I can't get a cab.

00:18:02.257 --> 00:18:04.343 line:80%
It's a 15-minute drive.
Please give me a ride.

00:18:04.426 --> 00:18:06.470 line:80%
-[Chan] Well, I…
-[panting]

00:18:06.553 --> 00:18:08.263 line:80%
But I…

00:18:08.347 --> 00:18:09.515 line:80%
-[panting] Yeah?
-[car honks]

00:18:10.516 --> 00:18:12.351 line:80%
[chuckles awkwardly] All right.

00:18:20.275 --> 00:18:21.276 line:80%
[sighs]

00:18:22.611 --> 00:18:25.280 line:80%
Do you know you're driving
20 km an hour right now?

00:18:25.364 --> 00:18:27.282 line:80%
You can drive up to 60 here.

00:18:27.366 --> 00:18:31.078 line:80%
I'm sorry, but can't you go a bit faster?
I only have 20 minutes left.

00:18:32.705 --> 00:18:34.206 line:80%
-Okay.
-[sighs]

00:18:34.999 --> 00:18:37.376 line:80%
[car honking]

00:18:37.459 --> 00:18:39.628 line:80%
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[♪ tense music playing]

00:18:39.712 --> 00:18:41.630 line:80%
-[tires screeching]
-Watch out!

00:18:44.091 --> 00:18:45.092 line:80%
[tires screech]

00:18:47.219 --> 00:18:49.221 line:80%
-[car honking]
-[breathing shakily]

00:18:50.931 --> 00:18:52.308 line:80%
[motorcycle driver] Hey!

00:18:52.433 --> 00:18:54.226 line:80%
Hey, get out.

00:18:55.561 --> 00:18:57.521 line:80%
Get out of the car.

00:18:57.604 --> 00:18:58.605 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:19:02.318 --> 00:19:04.611 line:80%
-[sighs]
-I almost got hit because of you.

00:19:04.695 --> 00:19:06.905 line:80%
-You can't just cut in like that.
-[stutters]

00:19:07.448 --> 00:19:11.076 line:80%
I'm sorry. I'll take care of any damages.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:12.661 line:80%
Uh…

00:19:13.829 --> 00:19:16.123 line:80%
Okay. I'll pick it up right away.

00:19:16.206 --> 00:19:17.583 line:80%
I'm so sorry.

00:19:20.627 --> 00:19:23.005 line:80%
[motorcycle engine revving]

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:28.302 line:80%
[breathes deeply]

00:19:33.432 --> 00:19:35.768 line:80%
[grunts] Ms. Song, look at me.

00:19:37.436 --> 00:19:38.854 line:80%
I'm sorry about that.

00:19:38.937 --> 00:19:40.189 line:80%
But everything's fine.

00:19:40.272 --> 00:19:42.816 line:80%
I took care of everything. It's fine.

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:45.277 line:80%
Are you okay?
Are you sure you're not hurt?

00:19:45.361 --> 00:19:48.989 line:80%
[gasping] I shouldn't have
asked you for a ride.

00:19:49.865 --> 00:19:52.409 line:80%
Nothing happened,
and no one's hurt. It's fine.

00:19:53.243 --> 00:19:56.163 line:80%
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[Haran sighs]

00:19:56.246 --> 00:19:57.665 line:80%
MS. KIM

00:19:58.415 --> 00:20:01.293 line:80%
I'm sorry, but I don't think
I can take you. Uh…

00:20:02.336 --> 00:20:05.714 line:80%
There's a cab over there.
You're in a hurry, so go.

00:20:05.798 --> 00:20:08.926 line:80%
I'll take care of everything here,
so don't worry.

00:20:09.009 --> 00:20:10.886 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:20:12.096 --> 00:20:14.807 line:20%
[Haran] <i>Getting close to someone</i>
<i>is really difficult…</i>

00:20:15.391 --> 00:20:17.726 line:80%
<i>-No, it's scary for me.</i>
-[sighs]

00:20:18.811 --> 00:20:20.938 line:80%
If no one is special to me,

00:20:21.981 --> 00:20:24.274 line:80%
then at least nothing bad will happen.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:25.901 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:20:39.081 --> 00:20:40.124 line:80%
[gasps]

00:20:43.711 --> 00:20:44.795 line:80%
[both] Earlier…

00:20:46.422 --> 00:20:47.423 line:80%
[sighs]

00:20:49.717 --> 00:20:53.053 line:80%
[exhales heavily]
I'm sorry about what happened earlier.

00:20:53.137 --> 00:20:56.890 line:80%
No, I'm sorry.
I shouldn't have forced you like that.

00:20:58.976 --> 00:21:00.561 line:80%
It was because of your ear, right?

00:21:01.979 --> 00:21:03.897 line:80%
It seemed that way.

00:21:03.981 --> 00:21:04.982 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:21:05.065 --> 00:21:06.734 line:80%
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[car honk echoes]

00:21:06.817 --> 00:21:08.569 line:80%
[tires screech]

00:21:10.529 --> 00:21:14.325 line:80%
A few years ago,
Ben got injured because of me.

00:21:14.408 --> 00:21:16.535 line:80%
There was a honk on my left side,

00:21:17.745 --> 00:21:19.330 line:80%
but I couldn't react properly,

00:21:20.205 --> 00:21:21.290 line:80%
like earlier.

00:21:23.334 --> 00:21:27.921 line:80%
Since then, I told myself
I would never give anyone a ride,

00:21:29.006 --> 00:21:30.341 line:80%
but…

00:21:30.424 --> 00:21:34.219 line:80%
Today was the first time,
so I guess I was anxious.

00:21:35.637 --> 00:21:36.847 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:38.349 line:80%
You're scared

00:21:39.433 --> 00:21:40.684 line:80%
of bad things happening,

00:21:41.352 --> 00:21:42.770 line:80%
but I made you go through that.

00:21:47.232 --> 00:21:50.527 line:80%
Your free trial
is proving to be effective, though.

00:21:52.488 --> 00:21:56.241 line:80%
Back at the Hangang River,
and in the car earlier,

00:21:56.825 --> 00:21:58.202 line:80%
it helped me a lot.

00:21:58.285 --> 00:22:00.287 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:22:02.956 --> 00:22:06.627 line:80%
I don't exactly have good memories
about Jamsugyo.

00:22:09.838 --> 00:22:12.925 line:80%
<i>I thought I'd only have sad memories</i>
<i>about it forever,</i>

00:22:13.008 --> 00:22:14.468 line:80%
<i>but I realized I could smile there.</i>

00:22:15.094 --> 00:22:20.057 line:80%
Perhaps I can overwrite
those sad memories, too.

00:22:21.308 --> 00:22:22.893 line:80%
I thought that for the first time.

00:22:23.978 --> 00:22:28.482 line:80%
And I was really scared back in the car,
but I recovered quickly thanks to you.

00:22:30.192 --> 00:22:33.612 line:80%
If it were a few days ago,
I would have just tried to flee again.

00:22:34.989 --> 00:22:36.115 line:80%
But I won't now.

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:40.369 line:80%
At least until the trial is over,

00:22:40.452 --> 00:22:42.079 line:80%
I won't enter my cave again.

00:22:43.622 --> 00:22:47.126 line:80%
So don't blame yourself, okay?

00:22:53.382 --> 00:22:55.759 line:80%
[inhales sharply, sighs] I'm relieved.

00:22:57.720 --> 00:22:58.804 line:80%
To be honest,

00:23:00.139 --> 00:23:01.890 line:80%
I was pretty scared.

00:23:03.684 --> 00:23:05.394 line:80%
You just mustered up your courage,

00:23:06.729 --> 00:23:08.772 line:80%
and I was worried you'd run away again.

00:23:09.982 --> 00:23:11.859 line:80%
I said we'd have fun,

00:23:12.526 --> 00:23:16.113 line:80%
but I thought I'd already ruined it.

00:23:16.655 --> 00:23:17.781 line:80%
[Chan chuckles softly]

00:23:18.407 --> 00:23:19.867 line:80%
Keep teaching me.

00:23:19.950 --> 00:23:21.994 line:80%
I'll do my best to learn.

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:29.752 line:80%
I'll get going now. Bye.

00:23:29.835 --> 00:23:31.295 line:80%
Okay. Bye.

00:23:31.378 --> 00:23:32.379 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:23:33.505 --> 00:23:34.590 line:80%
Ah.

00:23:34.673 --> 00:23:36.050 line:80%
I actually don't like…

00:23:37.426 --> 00:23:39.720 line:80%
everything being okay and only having fun.

00:23:40.304 --> 00:23:42.056 line:80%
That's fake friendship.

00:23:43.390 --> 00:23:45.643 line:80%
Being able to tell each other
when you're not okay

00:23:45.726 --> 00:23:46.935 line:80%
is real friendship, right?

00:23:48.312 --> 00:23:49.563 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:23:49.647 --> 00:23:52.483 line:80%
So let's tell each other in advance
if something's wrong

00:23:52.566 --> 00:23:54.652 line:80%
so we won't have to feel guilty
like today.

00:23:55.611 --> 00:23:58.072 line:80%
All right. [inhales sharply]

00:23:58.155 --> 00:24:00.824 line:80%
But you should stop that
if you want real friendship.

00:24:00.908 --> 00:24:02.159 line:80%
Stop what?

00:24:04.203 --> 00:24:07.164 line:80%
You don't have to worry so much
about my hearing.

00:24:07.706 --> 00:24:08.916 line:80%
What? Me?

00:24:08.999 --> 00:24:10.167 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:14.046 line:80%
-I wasn't worried about that at all.
-[chuckles] It's pretty obvious, you know.

00:24:14.630 --> 00:24:18.592 line:80%
Ever since you found out,
you've been standing to my right.

00:24:19.468 --> 00:24:23.847 line:80%
I'm usually fine,
so you don't have to do that, okay?

00:24:23.931 --> 00:24:28.894 line:80%
Well, it's been a long time
since I made a new friend,

00:24:29.561 --> 00:24:33.440 line:80%
so I'm not really sure what I have to do.

00:24:33.524 --> 00:24:34.775 line:80%
You seem mature,

00:24:35.901 --> 00:24:37.152 line:80%
but you're a picky eater.

00:24:37.236 --> 00:24:39.613 line:80%
You love Mr. Park's coffee,

00:24:40.197 --> 00:24:42.491 line:80%
you ride a bike very well,

00:24:43.409 --> 00:24:46.120 line:80%
and you pretend not to be,
but you're pretty caring.

00:24:47.121 --> 00:24:48.122 line:80%
What?

00:24:48.205 --> 00:24:49.832 line:80%
This is how you become friends.

00:24:51.125 --> 00:24:53.043 line:80%
Slowly, without forcing anything,

00:24:53.127 --> 00:24:55.587 line:80%
by finding out small things
about each other.

00:24:57.840 --> 00:25:00.759 line:80%
I also don't like oysters.
They're like snot.

00:25:00.843 --> 00:25:02.761 line:80%
What? Snot?

00:25:02.845 --> 00:25:04.513 line:80%
I just told you more about myself.

00:25:06.432 --> 00:25:08.809 line:80%
-Is this not how you do it?
-[chuckles]

00:25:10.311 --> 00:25:11.603 line:80%
It is. That's right.

00:25:11.687 --> 00:25:13.564 line:80%
Give me your hand. I'll give you a stamp.

00:25:14.898 --> 00:25:16.734 line:80%
Here. A "great job" stamp.

00:25:18.736 --> 00:25:19.862 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:25:19.945 --> 00:25:22.865 line:80%
I told you a secret,
so next time it's your turn.

00:25:25.784 --> 00:25:29.580 line:80%
It doesn't have to be anything big.
Just a small one.

00:25:30.039 --> 00:25:31.040 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:25:31.123 --> 00:25:32.124 line:80%
Bye, then.

00:25:34.710 --> 00:25:35.794 line:80%
Bye.

00:25:39.882 --> 00:25:41.550 line:80%
[inhales sharply, sighs]

00:25:41.633 --> 00:25:42.634 line:80%
A secret…

00:25:44.595 --> 00:25:45.596 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:25:46.513 --> 00:25:47.514 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:25:50.976 --> 00:25:52.936 line:80%
[Hadam] Hmm. Hair, check.

00:25:53.020 --> 00:25:56.065 line:80%
Your outfit's nice… [squeals]
and your face is even nicer.

00:25:56.148 --> 00:25:58.734 line:80%
-You're perfect.
-[sighs wearily]

00:25:58.817 --> 00:26:00.361 line:80%
I'm so nervous.

00:26:00.444 --> 00:26:02.946 line:80%
I wasn't even this nervous
at the Comets press conference.

00:26:03.030 --> 00:26:05.449 line:80%
It's okay to be nervous.

00:26:05.532 --> 00:26:06.825 line:80%
Just be yourself.

00:26:06.909 --> 00:26:10.746 line:80%
Wow. Hearing you say that
suddenly made me calm.

00:26:10.829 --> 00:26:13.624 line:80%
[chuckles softly] Then hold my hand.

00:26:16.585 --> 00:26:18.045 line:80%
[whines]

00:26:18.128 --> 00:26:21.173 line:80%
I'm actually really nervous. [giggles]

00:26:22.508 --> 00:26:24.718 line:80%
Just trust me. Let's do this.

00:26:25.552 --> 00:26:27.137 line:80%
-Okay.
-[door opens]

00:26:29.390 --> 00:26:30.891 line:80%
You're finally here.

00:26:30.975 --> 00:26:33.143 line:80%
Let's see who this guy is.

00:26:34.061 --> 00:26:35.980 line:80%
Hello. I'm Cha Yougyum.

00:26:38.691 --> 00:26:40.317 line:80%
[♪ pensive music playing]

00:26:41.485 --> 00:26:43.445 line:80%
-[traffic light beeping]
-[Yougyum] <i>It's a green light!</i>

00:26:44.321 --> 00:26:45.322 line:80%
[grunts]

00:26:46.073 --> 00:26:47.241 line:80%
[sighs]

00:26:47.324 --> 00:26:48.951 line:80%
[car horns honking]

00:26:49.034 --> 00:26:50.202 line:80%
[exclaiming]

00:26:50.285 --> 00:26:51.453 line:80%
[car honks]

00:26:54.123 --> 00:26:55.207 line:80%
-[tires screech]
-[car honks loudly]

00:26:55.290 --> 00:26:57.710 line:80%
[cars honking]

00:26:58.877 --> 00:27:01.463 line:80%
Why did you get here late?

00:27:01.547 --> 00:27:03.173 line:80%
Who did you help?

00:27:04.008 --> 00:27:05.009 line:80%
[Yougyum] <i>An elderly woman.</i>

00:27:05.718 --> 00:27:09.263 line:80%
<i>She was standing in the middle</i>
<i>of the crosswalk at a red light.</i>

00:27:09.346 --> 00:27:10.639 line:80%
<i>It looked dangerous.</i>

00:27:10.723 --> 00:27:13.350 line:80%
Are you all right, ma'am?
Where are you headed?

00:27:14.560 --> 00:27:17.062 line:80%
<i>It seemed like she might have dementia.</i>

00:27:18.605 --> 00:27:19.815 line:80%
-[♪ music continues]
-Oh…

00:27:26.905 --> 00:27:27.906 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:27:27.990 --> 00:27:29.450 line:80%
[gasps, exclaims]

00:27:29.533 --> 00:27:32.077 line:80%
It's nice to meet you. [chuckles]

00:27:32.578 --> 00:27:35.331 line:80%
Hadam doesn't know,
so pretend you never saw me.

00:27:38.792 --> 00:27:39.793 line:80%
[giggles]

00:27:39.877 --> 00:27:41.337 line:80%
Isn't he handsome?

00:27:42.004 --> 00:27:43.005 line:80%
[Hadam giggles]

00:27:44.131 --> 00:27:46.592 line:80%
What? Yougyum, are you crying?

00:27:47.176 --> 00:27:49.094 line:80%
-Huh?
-[♪ amusing music playing]

00:27:49.178 --> 00:27:51.055 line:80%
[chuckling nervously] Oh, I…

00:27:51.138 --> 00:27:54.266 line:80%
[stuttering] I'm just so happy
to meet your grandmother.

00:27:55.517 --> 00:27:56.769 line:80%
I couldn't help it.

00:27:56.852 --> 00:27:58.854 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:28:14.953 --> 00:28:15.954 line:80%
[Hadam sighs]

00:28:16.705 --> 00:28:18.707 line:80%
-[line ringing]
-Why aren't they picking up?

00:28:20.417 --> 00:28:21.418 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:28:21.502 --> 00:28:23.504 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[line disconnects]

00:28:27.800 --> 00:28:30.886 line:80%
My sisters aren't picking up.
We should just…

00:28:32.971 --> 00:28:34.640 line:80%
Why are you sweating?

00:28:35.808 --> 00:28:37.726 line:80%
-Is it hot?
-Oh.

00:28:39.311 --> 00:28:40.896 line:80%
I'm not feeling so well.

00:28:42.731 --> 00:28:44.650 line:80%
I'll come back when her sisters are here.

00:28:44.733 --> 00:28:46.110 line:80%
-What?
-Will you?

00:28:47.111 --> 00:28:48.445 line:80%
I'll see you again next time.

00:28:48.529 --> 00:28:49.613 line:80%
See you at school.

00:28:50.197 --> 00:28:51.824 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:28:52.700 --> 00:28:53.701 line:80%
[Hadam] Yougyum!

00:28:57.663 --> 00:28:59.081 line:80%
What was that, Grandma?

00:28:59.164 --> 00:29:02.251 line:80%
You didn't even look at him
and didn't say a word. [groans]

00:29:02.334 --> 00:29:04.378 line:80%
He left because
you made him uncomfortable.

00:29:04.461 --> 00:29:05.629 line:80%
Hadam.

00:29:05.713 --> 00:29:07.715 line:80%
I'm not feeling well today, either--

00:29:07.798 --> 00:29:09.466 line:80%
Haran and Hayeong didn't even come.

00:29:09.550 --> 00:29:11.719 line:80%
He's really important to me.
How can you do this?

00:29:11.802 --> 00:29:14.304 line:80%
Did you think I was joking
about getting married?

00:29:14.388 --> 00:29:16.098 line:80%
-Hadam.
-I can't believe this!

00:29:16.181 --> 00:29:17.641 line:80%
[breathing heavily]

00:29:17.725 --> 00:29:19.518 line:80%
-Yougyum!
-Hadam!

00:29:21.061 --> 00:29:23.063 line:80%
-[door opens, closes]
-[sighs]

00:29:23.981 --> 00:29:26.734 line:80%
How could he be… [sighs]

00:29:36.285 --> 00:29:37.286 line:80%
Hayeong!

00:29:37.369 --> 00:29:39.872 line:80%
-Why are you so late?
-Well, I…

00:29:39.955 --> 00:29:41.415 line:80%
-There's chalk on your face.
-Yougyum!

00:29:41.498 --> 00:29:42.499 line:80%
[Hayeong mumbles]

00:29:42.583 --> 00:29:43.584 line:80%
[Haran] Hadam!

00:29:44.460 --> 00:29:45.461 line:80%
Did Yougyum leave?

00:29:46.670 --> 00:29:49.923 line:80%
I'm sorry, things were hectic.
I didn't notice the time.

00:29:50.007 --> 00:29:51.342 line:80%
I'm really sorry, too.

00:29:51.425 --> 00:29:53.302 line:80%
We have a fitting tomorrow,
but the sample--

00:29:53.385 --> 00:29:55.429 line:80%
Right. Sure.

00:29:55.512 --> 00:29:57.264 line:80%
I'm sure you had your reasons.

00:29:58.057 --> 00:29:59.058 line:80%
It's fine.

00:29:59.141 --> 00:30:01.226 line:80%
You're so generous.

00:30:01.310 --> 00:30:02.686 line:80%
You have a big heart…

00:30:02.770 --> 00:30:04.605 line:80%
-Or maybe not.
-[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:30:04.688 --> 00:30:07.066 line:80%
You're not okay, are you?

00:30:07.149 --> 00:30:08.651 line:80%
You're angry, right?

00:30:08.734 --> 00:30:10.319 line:80%
Yes. Very.

00:30:11.445 --> 00:30:14.740 line:80%
I'm holding back my anger,
so don't talk to me.

00:30:21.622 --> 00:30:25.834 line:80%
Are you jealous because I'm doing
way better than you? [groans angrily]

00:30:25.918 --> 00:30:27.044 line:80%
You're so annoying!

00:30:34.635 --> 00:30:36.470 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[Hayeong] Oh, no…

00:30:38.305 --> 00:30:41.850 line:80%
[door thuds, opens]

00:30:41.934 --> 00:30:44.395 line:80%
Grandma, why did Yougyum leave so quickly?

00:30:44.979 --> 00:30:47.523 line:80%
Um… He must not be feeling well.

00:30:48.440 --> 00:30:50.818 line:80%
[grunts] I should go shower. Go upstairs.

00:30:52.653 --> 00:30:53.821 line:80%
What?

00:30:53.904 --> 00:30:57.116 line:80%
Doesn't Grandma seem like she's unwell?

00:30:57.199 --> 00:30:59.159 line:80%
Maybe the lecture was pretty tough.

00:31:08.669 --> 00:31:10.170 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:31:10.254 --> 00:31:12.256 line:80%
-[traffic light beeping]
-[indistinct chatter]

00:31:24.810 --> 00:31:26.145 line:80%
[car honk echoes]

00:31:26.770 --> 00:31:27.771 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:31:41.201 --> 00:31:42.411 line:80%
[car honk echoes]

00:31:44.705 --> 00:31:47.124 line:80%
Are you all right, ma'am?
Where are you headed?

00:31:48.709 --> 00:31:51.420 line:80%
[grunts softly] I'm not sure.

00:31:52.004 --> 00:31:54.965 line:80%
I can't remember where I was going.

00:31:59.678 --> 00:32:02.681 line:80%
It's okay. We'll cross the street together
when it's a green light.

00:32:19.657 --> 00:32:21.867 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-[sighs]

00:32:23.160 --> 00:32:24.161 line:80%
[sniffles]

00:32:28.916 --> 00:32:30.292 line:80%
Hadam. I'm sorry.

00:32:30.376 --> 00:32:32.628 line:80%
Tell Yougyum to come back next time, okay?

00:32:35.923 --> 00:32:37.257 line:80%
[sighs defeatedly]

00:32:41.428 --> 00:32:42.429 line:80%
[sniffles]

00:32:48.060 --> 00:32:49.144 line:80%
[sniffs]

00:32:49.228 --> 00:32:51.063 line:80%
-[♪ soft emotional music playing]
-[exhales]

00:32:53.357 --> 00:32:54.358 line:80%
[sniffles]

00:32:58.904 --> 00:33:02.157 line:80%
[deep inhale, sighs]

00:33:09.248 --> 00:33:10.332 line:80%
[sighs]

00:33:12.710 --> 00:33:13.711 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:33:16.130 --> 00:33:17.881 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:33:18.507 --> 00:33:19.508 line:80%
Yes, Mr. Cha.

00:33:20.134 --> 00:33:21.218 line:80%
Lunch?

00:33:21.301 --> 00:33:23.512 line:80%
I'd love that. I'll head there now.

00:33:23.595 --> 00:33:25.889 line:80%
-Okay.
-Ms. Song.

00:33:25.973 --> 00:33:27.016 line:80%
Yes?

00:33:33.605 --> 00:33:34.815 line:80%
Ms. Kim is asking for you.

00:33:34.898 --> 00:33:36.233 line:80%
Me?

00:33:36.942 --> 00:33:37.943 line:80%
[gasps]

00:33:38.986 --> 00:33:42.906 line:80%
Wait. I went there last time,
but she'd already gone home.

00:33:42.990 --> 00:33:45.617 line:80%
Why do you keep playing pranks?
It doesn't suit you.

00:33:45.701 --> 00:33:48.203 line:80%
I mixed up the date.
She wanted to see you today.

00:33:48.287 --> 00:33:50.664 line:80%
You should go see her now.

00:33:50.748 --> 00:33:51.832 line:80%
You mean it?

00:33:51.915 --> 00:33:53.125 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:33:53.208 --> 00:33:56.170 line:80%
[sighs] All right, then.

00:33:59.381 --> 00:34:01.133 line:80%
Yes, Mr. Cha.

00:34:01.216 --> 00:34:04.720 line:80%
I don't think I can go. I'm sorry.

00:34:05.637 --> 00:34:08.182 line:20%
I don't know. She keeps asking for me.

00:34:08.265 --> 00:34:09.642 line:20%
MEN'S HEALTH
SEONGWON BRANCH

00:34:11.143 --> 00:34:12.144 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:34:15.981 --> 00:34:18.192 line:80%
-[footsteps approaching]
-[knock on door]

00:34:18.275 --> 00:34:20.402 line:80%
[exclaims softly] Just a minute.

00:34:20.986 --> 00:34:22.112 line:80%
Come in.

00:34:22.196 --> 00:34:24.156 line:80%
Ms. Kim.

00:34:24.239 --> 00:34:26.241 line:80%
I heard you asked for me.

00:34:26.325 --> 00:34:28.327 line:80%
Were you dreaming? I didn't ask for you.

00:34:28.869 --> 00:34:31.163 line:80%
-Get out. Don't bother me.
-Eh?

00:34:31.246 --> 00:34:34.708 line:80%
What's with Mr. Yeon?
Why does he keep lying to me?

00:34:34.792 --> 00:34:36.585 line:80%
I'd like you to talk to yourself outside.

00:34:36.669 --> 00:34:37.878 line:80%
Okay.

00:34:38.462 --> 00:34:39.922 line:80%
I'll excuse myself, then.

00:34:41.882 --> 00:34:44.593 line:80%
-[door opens, closes]
-[footsteps leaving]

00:34:44.677 --> 00:34:46.011 line:80%
Did I ask for her?

00:34:46.970 --> 00:34:47.971 line:80%
I don't think I did.

00:34:49.848 --> 00:34:51.433 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:35:00.859 --> 00:35:02.861 line:80%
[♪ mysterious music plays]

00:35:09.618 --> 00:35:10.619 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:35:10.703 --> 00:35:13.205 line:80%
Sol, the shoulder is 17 inches, right?

00:35:13.288 --> 00:35:15.708 line:80%
-[Sol] Oh. One moment, please.
-[Hayeong] Okay.

00:35:16.834 --> 00:35:18.877 line:80%
What's going on? Something's off.

00:35:19.920 --> 00:35:22.256 line:80%
Something's different from usual.

00:35:22.339 --> 00:35:24.341 line:80%
What? What's different?

00:35:25.300 --> 00:35:26.301 line:80%
[Remy] What?

00:35:29.388 --> 00:35:30.931 line:80%
-[screams]
-[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:35:31.015 --> 00:35:32.057 line:80%
Right. It's that.

00:35:32.141 --> 00:35:34.268 line:80%
She hasn't pushed the button once today.

00:35:34.351 --> 00:35:35.519 line:80%
-[gasps]
-[Sol exclaims]

00:35:35.602 --> 00:35:37.062 line:80%
You're right!

00:35:46.780 --> 00:35:47.781 line:80%
[both exclaim]

00:35:47.865 --> 00:35:49.408 line:80%
-[Seung-gyu] Are you okay?
-[Sol] I'm sorry.

00:35:49.491 --> 00:35:50.701 line:80%
[mumbling]

00:35:50.784 --> 00:35:51.994 line:80%
[Remy] Two, four…

00:35:52.077 --> 00:35:54.079 line:80%
-Look at the time.
-[♪ music fades]

00:35:54.747 --> 00:35:56.790 line:80%
-[staff chatter indistinctly]
-What a surprise.

00:35:58.083 --> 00:35:59.460 line:80%
[Haran] <i>What? Gyeongju?</i>

00:35:59.543 --> 00:36:01.128 line:80%
The costume team, too?

00:36:01.211 --> 00:36:03.464 line:80%
Yes, it was our director's idea.

00:36:03.547 --> 00:36:05.341 line:80%
He said a better understanding
of the background

00:36:05.424 --> 00:36:07.509 line:80%
would help with the costumes.

00:36:07.593 --> 00:36:08.761 line:80%
Right.

00:36:09.470 --> 00:36:12.473 line:80%
We won't be able to capture the details
with the script alone.

00:36:13.223 --> 00:36:14.224 line:80%
Then shall we…

00:36:14.975 --> 00:36:16.810 line:80%
[whooshing]

00:36:18.062 --> 00:36:19.063 line:80%
Ah.

00:36:19.146 --> 00:36:21.607 line:80%
My schedule's packed,

00:36:21.690 --> 00:36:24.652 line:80%
so you can go as long as
it doesn't interfere with other work.

00:36:24.735 --> 00:36:26.695 line:80%
I'm ready to go!

00:36:26.779 --> 00:36:29.823 line:80%
I've been buried in fabric dust.
I'll finally get some fresh air!

00:36:29.907 --> 00:36:32.910 line:80%
You're not going on a picnic.
Get fresh air on your day off.

00:36:34.119 --> 00:36:36.330 line:80%
You know I'll work hard there.

00:36:36.413 --> 00:36:37.665 line:80%
Picnic, beep.

00:36:37.748 --> 00:36:41.377 line:80%
Business trip, ding ding ding. [chuckles]

00:36:41.460 --> 00:36:44.421 line:80%
I think two nights will be enough
for your team. Is that okay?

00:36:44.922 --> 00:36:48.509 line:80%
Then our costume team
will head there on Thursday.

00:36:48.592 --> 00:36:49.677 line:80%
All right.

00:36:55.683 --> 00:36:57.685 line:80%
[♪ upbeat song playing over speakers]

00:37:08.153 --> 00:37:09.530 line:80%
[mumbling]

00:37:11.407 --> 00:37:12.700 line:80%
Hey, Yang Changmo!

00:37:13.742 --> 00:37:14.910 line:80%
Hey, Hadam.

00:37:16.704 --> 00:37:17.788 line:80%
Where's Yougyum?

00:37:17.871 --> 00:37:19.289 line:80%
He said he had to go somewhere.

00:37:19.373 --> 00:37:22.668 line:80%
Oh… Wasn't he meeting up with you?

00:37:23.669 --> 00:37:24.670 line:80%
Huh?

00:37:27.840 --> 00:37:29.633 line:80%
How are we going to get through today?

00:37:29.717 --> 00:37:30.926 line:80%
We do it every day.

00:37:31.010 --> 00:37:32.136 line:80%
Yougyum!

00:37:32.219 --> 00:37:33.303 line:80%
Hey.

00:37:33.387 --> 00:37:34.638 line:80%
Go ahead.

00:37:35.848 --> 00:37:37.099 line:80%
Sorry about yesterday.

00:37:37.766 --> 00:37:39.393 line:80%
Let's talk after your practice.

00:37:39.476 --> 00:37:43.147 line:80%
No, I'm sorry.
I didn't take care of myself properly.

00:37:44.273 --> 00:37:47.776 line:80%
But sorry, Changmo asked to see me later.

00:37:47.860 --> 00:37:51.822 line:80%
Maybe he needs my advice
on something. [chuckles awkwardly]

00:37:53.115 --> 00:37:54.116 line:80%
[Hadam chuckles softly]

00:37:55.534 --> 00:37:57.494 line:80%
Yougyum, what are you doing?

00:37:58.787 --> 00:38:00.581 line:80%
You said you're meeting Changmo.

00:38:01.457 --> 00:38:02.583 line:80%
Did you meet him?

00:38:02.666 --> 00:38:04.710 line:80%
[Yougyum] <i>What? Yes, why?</i>

00:38:05.210 --> 00:38:07.046 line:80%
<i>-Is something up?</i>
-Huh?

00:38:07.129 --> 00:38:08.130 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:38:08.213 --> 00:38:10.132 line:80%
No, I was just calling.

00:38:11.133 --> 00:38:12.509 line:80%
Bye, then.

00:38:13.093 --> 00:38:14.094 line:80%
[line disconnects]

00:38:20.934 --> 00:38:21.935 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:38:29.902 --> 00:38:30.903 line:80%
Oh?

00:38:31.487 --> 00:38:32.863 line:80%
Yougyum…

00:38:32.946 --> 00:38:34.156 line:80%
Yougyum!

00:38:45.709 --> 00:38:47.002 line:80%
[Sora] I'll see you later.

00:38:54.510 --> 00:38:56.095 line:80%
I wanted to meet you, too.

00:38:56.178 --> 00:38:57.888 line:80%
Are you happy? Enjoying your date?

00:38:58.973 --> 00:39:01.350 line:80%
-Hadam!
-How could you meet Han Sora--

00:39:01.433 --> 00:39:02.476 line:80%
-[♪ music ends]
-[woman] Hadam.

00:39:04.269 --> 00:39:05.270 line:80%
[Hadam gasps]

00:39:05.354 --> 00:39:08.065 line:80%
-What are you doing here?
-I'm here too.

00:39:11.026 --> 00:39:13.904 line:80%
What? You were waiting
in front of our school?

00:39:13.988 --> 00:39:15.364 line:80%
You didn't even know his face.

00:39:15.447 --> 00:39:18.867 line:20%
How could we not know him?
He was even on the news.

00:39:18.951 --> 00:39:20.869 line:80%
-[chuckles shyly]
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:39:20.953 --> 00:39:22.246 line:80%
They threatened you, didn't they?

00:39:22.830 --> 00:39:25.374 line:80%
That's why you lied to me, right?

00:39:25.457 --> 00:39:29.003 line:80%
I told him not to tell you
because we wanted to apologize.

00:39:29.086 --> 00:39:30.879 line:80%
No, there's no need.

00:39:30.963 --> 00:39:33.132 line:80%
I left early
because I wasn't feeling well.

00:39:34.174 --> 00:39:38.303 line:80%
But who's Han Sora?
You said something about Han Sora.

00:39:38.387 --> 00:39:42.766 line:80%
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:39:42.850 --> 00:39:45.144 line:80%
[exclaims softly] Let's eat.

00:39:47.896 --> 00:39:48.897 line:80%
[gasps]

00:39:48.981 --> 00:39:51.150 line:80%
[Hadam] Mmm. This is good.

00:39:51.233 --> 00:39:53.068 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:39:53.152 --> 00:39:54.194 line:80%
Hey, Hadam.

00:39:54.737 --> 00:39:56.822 line:80%
-[Hadam] <i>You said you're meeting Changmo.</i>
-Huh?

00:39:57.406 --> 00:39:58.615 line:80%
<i>Did you meet him?</i>

00:39:58.699 --> 00:40:01.327 line:80%
What? Yes, why? Is something up?

00:40:01.410 --> 00:40:04.038 line:80%
<i>Huh? No, I was just calling.</i>

00:40:04.705 --> 00:40:06.457 line:80%
[sighs softly] Okay.

00:40:08.292 --> 00:40:09.293 line:80%
[line disconnects]

00:40:11.795 --> 00:40:13.505 line:80%
There's a visitor? Who…

00:40:19.595 --> 00:40:22.097 line:80%
[Yougyum] Is it pretty bad?

00:40:22.181 --> 00:40:24.558 line:80%
[Nana] My mind goes blank
from time to time.

00:40:24.642 --> 00:40:27.478 line:80%
I sometimes buy the same book
two or three times.

00:40:29.021 --> 00:40:33.067 line:80%
I'm usually fine,
but there are days I'm not,

00:40:35.235 --> 00:40:36.737 line:80%
like the day I met you.

00:40:37.988 --> 00:40:40.366 line:80%
Uh… Did you see a doctor?

00:40:42.076 --> 00:40:45.663 line:80%
I got a basic checkup,
and they said there were signs.

00:40:46.246 --> 00:40:49.583 line:80%
I scheduled a follow-up exam
in a few weeks.

00:40:51.710 --> 00:40:53.545 line:80%
But at my age,

00:40:55.214 --> 00:40:57.049 line:80%
you can sense it.

00:40:57.800 --> 00:41:00.177 line:80%
It's probably right.

00:41:00.260 --> 00:41:02.596 line:80%
-[♪ soft emotional music playing]
-[sighs]

00:41:03.514 --> 00:41:06.934 line:80%
I'm not sure what to do.

00:41:07.017 --> 00:41:08.769 line:80%
You should tell your family--

00:41:08.852 --> 00:41:09.937 line:80%
No.

00:41:10.020 --> 00:41:12.356 line:80%
I have to focus on what I can do now.

00:41:13.774 --> 00:41:17.528 line:80%
I don't know how much longer
I'll be myself.

00:41:17.611 --> 00:41:21.031 line:80%
I have to take care of things
and receive treatment while I can.

00:41:24.284 --> 00:41:27.830 line:80%
I'm sorry to burden you,
but please do me a favor.

00:41:28.789 --> 00:41:30.040 line:80%
[Hayeong] The fries here are good.

00:41:30.124 --> 00:41:31.875 line:80%
[Haran] Hadam, try this.
You like these, right?

00:41:31.959 --> 00:41:36.338 line:80%
[Nana] <i>Haran has already lost</i>
<i>many loved ones.</i>

00:41:36.964 --> 00:41:38.799 line:80%
<i>I don't want to be a burden to her now.</i>

00:41:39.633 --> 00:41:42.386 line:80%
<i>Hayeong is always so loud</i>
<i>and quick to laugh.</i>

00:41:42.469 --> 00:41:45.931 line:80%
<i>But if she finds out about my condition,</i>
<i>she won't be able to smile again.</i>

00:41:47.641 --> 00:41:49.018 line:80%
<i>Hadam's in her senior year.</i>

00:41:49.518 --> 00:41:52.980 line:80%
<i>She needs to focus on her studies.</i>
<i>I won't be the reason she falls apart.</i>

00:41:53.772 --> 00:41:55.190 line:80%
<i>So please...</i>

00:41:56.650 --> 00:41:57.651 line:80%
<i>For now,</i>

00:41:58.277 --> 00:42:00.362 line:80%
<i>keep this a secret.</i>

00:42:08.579 --> 00:42:10.581 line:80%
I don't have much time.

00:42:15.085 --> 00:42:16.086 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:42:16.670 --> 00:42:19.465 line:80%
[groans] How badly did they scrape it?

00:42:20.299 --> 00:42:23.218 line:80%
Are you the one who called me
about the accident?

00:42:23.302 --> 00:42:25.304 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:42:28.390 --> 00:42:31.226 line:80%
I did call you, but there was no accident.

00:42:31.310 --> 00:42:33.979 line:80%
What… Then why would you say
there was an accident?

00:42:35.064 --> 00:42:36.482 line:80%
Hang on.

00:42:36.565 --> 00:42:37.691 line:80%
It's you, isn't it?

00:42:37.775 --> 00:42:39.777 line:80%
-I have it all planned out.
-Mr. Cha Min?

00:42:42.279 --> 00:42:44.323 line:80%
[Min] I'll treat you to something nice.

00:42:44.406 --> 00:42:45.407 line:80%
[tires screeching]

00:42:45.491 --> 00:42:46.742 line:80%
-[exclaiming]
-[♪ music ends]

00:42:47.910 --> 00:42:49.078 line:80%
[tires screeching]

00:42:49.161 --> 00:42:50.579 line:80%
[window whirring]

00:42:54.917 --> 00:42:55.959 line:80%
[scoffs]

00:43:00.381 --> 00:43:02.383 line:80%
What was that? What's with him?

00:43:03.175 --> 00:43:05.761 line:80%
The guy in the hotel parking lot
who reversed into me.

00:43:05.844 --> 00:43:07.137 line:80%
Who are you--

00:43:07.221 --> 00:43:08.722 line:80%
That's not your business.

00:43:09.807 --> 00:43:13.852 line:80%
Why don't you sort out
all the women you've been juggling?

00:43:13.936 --> 00:43:17.022 line:80%
What are you saying?
Who are you to order me around?

00:43:17.106 --> 00:43:19.984 line:80%
It would be best
to say you got transferred abroad

00:43:20.067 --> 00:43:21.443 line:80%
so no one feels hurt.

00:43:21.527 --> 00:43:24.446 line:80%
If you don't stop acting like a scumbag,

00:43:26.156 --> 00:43:28.283 line:80%
we'll be meeting again.

00:43:28.867 --> 00:43:30.244 line:80%
-[scoffs]
-[car lock beeps]

00:43:31.245 --> 00:43:32.538 line:80%
[Min] Hey!

00:43:34.873 --> 00:43:37.167 line:80%
That's what you call being a scumbag.

00:43:37.251 --> 00:43:39.461 line:80%
Do you want the other one broken, too?

00:43:39.545 --> 00:43:42.256 line:80%
Whether you break it or not,
just sort out your women problem.

00:43:42.840 --> 00:43:45.592 line:80%
I suggest sending out DMs right now.

00:43:45.676 --> 00:43:49.471 line:80%
Mmm… [singsongs] No, thanks.

00:43:49.555 --> 00:43:51.682 line:80%
I'm not going to.

00:43:51.765 --> 00:43:54.310 line:80%
It's all because I'm popular.

00:43:54.393 --> 00:43:56.186 line:80%
What are you going to do? [gasps]

00:43:56.270 --> 00:43:57.271 line:80%
-[♪ amusing music playing]
-Oh…

00:43:57.354 --> 00:43:59.023 line:80%
Wait. Hey. Hey!

00:43:59.773 --> 00:44:01.358 line:80%
[exclaims] My phone.

00:44:01.942 --> 00:44:03.444 line:80%
[exclaims nervously]

00:44:03.527 --> 00:44:04.528 line:80%
Hey!

00:44:05.988 --> 00:44:07.406 line:80%
If you don't sort them out,

00:44:07.489 --> 00:44:09.325 line:80%
the next thing you'll lose…

00:44:11.285 --> 00:44:12.995 line:80%
won't be your phone.

00:44:20.044 --> 00:44:21.045 line:80%
[Min] Wait.

00:44:21.128 --> 00:44:22.504 line:80%
-Hang on.
-Hello.

00:44:23.297 --> 00:44:25.591 line:80%
I want to schedule a car repair.

00:44:26.175 --> 00:44:27.343 line:80%
My phone's in there.

00:44:27.426 --> 00:44:29.386 line:80%
-What are you doing?
-[whining]

00:44:29.470 --> 00:44:31.722 line:80%
-[♪ music ends]
-I'm heading out! [grunts]

00:44:32.806 --> 00:44:34.224 line:80%
-[car lock beeps]
-[shudders]

00:44:34.725 --> 00:44:36.644 line:80%
-Whoa. Oh…
-I'll drive.

00:44:36.727 --> 00:44:38.479 line:80%
[stutters] What are you doing here?

00:44:38.562 --> 00:44:40.022 line:80%
We're going to Gyeongju.

00:44:40.105 --> 00:44:42.149 line:80%
I'm going to Gyeongju,
but the costume team--

00:44:42.232 --> 00:44:43.442 line:80%
I'm going today, too.

00:44:43.525 --> 00:44:45.361 line:80%
Can you load my luggage?

00:44:45.444 --> 00:44:46.445 line:80%
Oh…

00:44:46.528 --> 00:44:48.322 line:80%
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]
-[car door closes]

00:44:48.405 --> 00:44:49.406 line:80%
Sure…

00:44:51.283 --> 00:44:52.493 line:80%
[Chan inhales sharply]

00:44:52.576 --> 00:44:53.577 line:80%
[Chan] Mmm…

00:44:54.828 --> 00:44:57.081 line:80%
Wow. I feel pretty happy.

00:44:57.164 --> 00:44:59.375 line:80%
You're worried about me.

00:45:00.084 --> 00:45:01.543 line:80%
Worried?

00:45:01.627 --> 00:45:02.628 line:80%
Me?

00:45:03.337 --> 00:45:07.549 line:80%
[clicks tongue] You were worried about
me driving after what happened last time.

00:45:07.633 --> 00:45:09.009 line:80%
When did I…

00:45:11.845 --> 00:45:13.597 line:80%
You're right. [sighs]

00:45:13.681 --> 00:45:16.308 line:80%
It must be your first time
driving on a highway in Korea.

00:45:17.810 --> 00:45:18.894 line:80%
Thanks.

00:45:21.897 --> 00:45:22.898 line:80%
[Haran clears throat]

00:45:22.982 --> 00:45:23.983 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:45:24.066 --> 00:45:26.652 line:80%
But do you usually do
field research for animations?

00:45:26.735 --> 00:45:27.778 line:80%
Of course.

00:45:28.404 --> 00:45:30.698 line:80%
-You know Arendelle, right?
-[♪ enchanting music playing]

00:45:30.781 --> 00:45:34.493 line:80%
That was based on
a lakeside town called Hallstatt.

00:45:34.576 --> 00:45:41.542 line:80%
And the ice castle was inspired
by a hotel built of ice in Quebec.

00:45:42.126 --> 00:45:44.003 line:80%
And Won is Korean,

00:45:44.086 --> 00:45:46.338 line:80%
so we're looking
for her background in Korea.

00:45:46.880 --> 00:45:49.633 line:80%
We have to decide
where she grew up and how

00:45:49.717 --> 00:45:52.094 line:80%
so we can blend that into the story.

00:45:52.177 --> 00:45:56.223 line:80%
You had the vibe of a local bum,
but you seem like a pro now.

00:45:56.307 --> 00:45:57.433 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-A local bum?

00:45:57.516 --> 00:45:58.934 line:80%
Geez.

00:45:59.018 --> 00:46:02.271 line:80%
I didn't want to say this myself,
but I'll just say it.

00:46:02.354 --> 00:46:04.356 line:80%
I'm pretty competent.

00:46:04.440 --> 00:46:06.191 line:80%
I get lots of job offers, too.

00:46:06.275 --> 00:46:07.609 line:80%
I meant it's nice

00:46:07.693 --> 00:46:10.279 line:80%
seeing you look so excited
talking about work.

00:46:12.239 --> 00:46:13.699 line:80%
-[chuckles]
-[cell phone vibrating]

00:46:13.782 --> 00:46:14.783 line:80%
Hang on.

00:46:14.867 --> 00:46:15.868 line:80%
[grunts]

00:46:16.535 --> 00:46:17.536 line:80%
Hey, Ben.

00:46:18.704 --> 00:46:19.872 line:80%
Well, we're…

00:46:19.955 --> 00:46:21.457 line:80%
We're almost halfway there.

00:46:22.291 --> 00:46:23.584 line:80%
We're almost halfway there.

00:46:24.168 --> 00:46:26.670 line:80%
Oh. I'm going with Ms. Song.

00:46:27.796 --> 00:46:29.048 line:80%
It just happened.

00:46:29.131 --> 00:46:30.174 line:80%
See you later.

00:46:30.257 --> 00:46:32.259 line:80%
-[inhales sharply, sighs]
-[line disconnects]

00:46:34.511 --> 00:46:36.639 line:80%
I can smell rain.

00:46:38.682 --> 00:46:40.684 line:80%
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:46:49.818 --> 00:46:51.362 line:80%
Is it a shower?

00:46:52.655 --> 00:46:53.656 line:80%
[Chan] Mmm.

00:46:54.156 --> 00:46:57.576 line:80%
But I heard it's the smell
of organic matter diffusing,

00:46:57.660 --> 00:46:59.119 line:80%
not the rain.

00:46:59.203 --> 00:47:01.246 line:80%
-What was it again?
-Petrichor.

00:47:01.330 --> 00:47:02.414 line:80%
Right, petrichor.

00:47:03.499 --> 00:47:05.084 line:80%
You're really good at this stuff.

00:47:05.167 --> 00:47:08.087 line:80%
You said something about hypochlorite
at the police station, too.

00:47:08.921 --> 00:47:11.173 line:80%
It seems like you majored
in engineering, not art.

00:47:17.554 --> 00:47:20.182 line:80%
Oh? It stopped. What's going on?

00:47:20.265 --> 00:47:21.350 line:80%
-[mumbles]
-Huh?

00:47:21.433 --> 00:47:22.559 line:80%
Is it not working?

00:47:23.060 --> 00:47:24.853 line:80%
No. Didn't they check this car?

00:47:24.937 --> 00:47:26.563 line:80%
I got it checked.

00:47:27.940 --> 00:47:30.401 line:80%
It's not raining much yet, though.

00:47:30.484 --> 00:47:31.694 line:80%
[thunder rumbles]

00:47:32.903 --> 00:47:33.988 line:80%
-What…
-[exclaims]

00:47:34.071 --> 00:47:36.115 line:80%
Wait. It's raining too much.

00:47:36.198 --> 00:47:37.658 line:80%
Just pull over to the side.

00:47:37.741 --> 00:47:38.951 line:80%
Pull over?

00:47:39.034 --> 00:47:41.453 line:80%
[Haran exclaiming nervously]

00:47:41.537 --> 00:47:42.830 line:80%
UNDER CONSTRUCTION
NO SHOULDER AHEAD

00:47:42.913 --> 00:47:45.249 line:80%
Huh? "No shoulder ahead"?

00:47:45.332 --> 00:47:46.667 line:80%
Then what do we do?

00:47:46.750 --> 00:47:48.627 line:80%
It's not like we can make a road.

00:47:48.711 --> 00:47:50.713 line:80%
-First…
-Check if there are any cars.

00:47:50.796 --> 00:47:52.381 line:80%
Hang on. I'll take care of it.

00:47:52.464 --> 00:47:53.549 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:47:53.632 --> 00:47:55.592 line:80%
Oh no. I can't see anything. What do I do?

00:47:55.676 --> 00:47:57.594 line:80%
Wait.

00:47:58.595 --> 00:48:00.306 line:80%
-Hang on.
-I can't see anything.

00:48:01.932 --> 00:48:03.350 line:80%
[exclaims, grunts]

00:48:03.434 --> 00:48:05.394 line:80%
-What are you doing?
-This won't work.

00:48:05.477 --> 00:48:07.187 line:80%
Check if there are any cars coming!

00:48:07.271 --> 00:48:08.314 line:80%
I can't see anything.

00:48:08.397 --> 00:48:09.732 line:80%
SOMUNGYEONG REST STOP

00:48:09.815 --> 00:48:11.608 line:80%
-It's a rest stop!
-A rest stop?

00:48:11.692 --> 00:48:13.193 line:80%
I can't see the road, though.

00:48:13.277 --> 00:48:17.573 line:80%
I'll keep my eye on the road,
so keep driving.

00:48:17.656 --> 00:48:18.657 line:80%
But I can't see.

00:48:18.741 --> 00:48:20.534 line:80%
I'll count to three,

00:48:20.617 --> 00:48:23.203 line:80%
-so turn right when I get to three.
-Okay.

00:48:23.287 --> 00:48:24.288 line:80%
[Chan] All right…

00:48:24.371 --> 00:48:26.415 line:80%
One, two,

00:48:27.333 --> 00:48:28.334 line:80%
three.

00:48:28.417 --> 00:48:29.752 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:48:33.172 --> 00:48:36.175 line:80%
SOMUNGYEONG REST STOP

00:48:36.759 --> 00:48:38.469 line:80%
[both sigh in relief]

00:48:39.428 --> 00:48:40.429 line:80%
[sighs]

00:48:42.306 --> 00:48:43.515 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:48:45.934 --> 00:48:46.935 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:48:49.897 --> 00:48:50.898 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:48:51.523 --> 00:48:52.608 line:80%
[Chan sighs]

00:48:55.736 --> 00:48:56.820 line:80%
Ah…

00:48:56.904 --> 00:48:58.530 line:80%
Take a breather.

00:48:58.614 --> 00:49:00.574 line:80%
I'll call the rental shop.

00:49:01.200 --> 00:49:02.409 line:80%
[Haran] Oh… [grunts]

00:49:07.414 --> 00:49:08.415 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:49:08.499 --> 00:49:10.626 line:80%
What? Four to five hours?

00:49:12.002 --> 00:49:13.295 line:80%
The motor's completely out.

00:49:13.379 --> 00:49:14.630 line:80%
We can't fix it here.

00:49:14.713 --> 00:49:16.799 line:80%
I'll take it to a repair shop nearby.

00:49:16.882 --> 00:49:20.302 line:80%
If you want a replacement,
we'll send you another car tomorrow.

00:49:20.886 --> 00:49:21.929 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:49:30.145 --> 00:49:32.564 line:80%
Yes, we probably won't get there
until tonight.

00:49:33.899 --> 00:49:36.568 line:80%
Okay, Ben. I'll call you again
when we're heading out.

00:49:37.194 --> 00:49:38.278 line:80%
Okay.

00:49:39.697 --> 00:49:40.698 line:80%
[line disconnects]

00:49:41.448 --> 00:49:42.449 line:80%
[shudders]

00:49:45.703 --> 00:49:47.079 line:80%
Here, wipe yourself up.

00:49:47.162 --> 00:49:48.664 line:80%
[stutters] It's fine.

00:49:49.581 --> 00:49:52.001 line:80%
-You really don't listen.
-[sighs]

00:49:54.253 --> 00:49:56.088 line:80%
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:50:07.975 --> 00:50:08.976 line:80%
[grunts]

00:50:11.312 --> 00:50:12.313 line:80%
[Haran sighs]

00:50:12.396 --> 00:50:14.523 line:80%
How are we going to wait here for hours?

00:50:16.525 --> 00:50:21.113 line:80%
There's someone in Mungyeong Saejae
I can ask for help.

00:50:21.196 --> 00:50:22.197 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:50:29.204 --> 00:50:30.706 line:80%
[tires screech]

00:50:34.710 --> 00:50:35.711 line:80%
Seonu Chan!

00:50:37.421 --> 00:50:39.715 line:80%
-[Chan] Wow, that was fast.
-[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:50:40.507 --> 00:50:42.968 line:80%
-You little brat.
-[groans]

00:50:43.052 --> 00:50:44.887 line:80%
You should've told me you came to Korea.

00:50:44.970 --> 00:50:47.306 line:80%
You only called me now?

00:50:47.389 --> 00:50:48.390 line:80%
Sorry.

00:50:48.474 --> 00:50:50.351 line:80%
-Oh, my. [gasps]
-[Chan chuckles]

00:50:50.434 --> 00:50:52.645 line:80%
-Did you take ginseng?
-Yes.

00:50:52.728 --> 00:50:54.980 line:80%
-You look so healthy.
-Right?

00:50:55.064 --> 00:50:56.732 line:80%
-[grunts]
-[chuckles]

00:50:56.815 --> 00:50:58.025 line:80%
Oh, dear.

00:50:58.776 --> 00:50:59.985 line:80%
Goodness.

00:51:00.069 --> 00:51:03.781 line:80%
This is Designer Song Haran,
who's working with me.

00:51:03.864 --> 00:51:05.032 line:80%
-Say hi.
-[sighs]

00:51:05.616 --> 00:51:07.117 line:80%
[Chan] She's my grandmother.

00:51:07.201 --> 00:51:08.202 line:80%
Grandmother?

00:51:08.285 --> 00:51:09.286 line:80%
Hello.

00:51:09.370 --> 00:51:10.621 line:80%
[Chan's grandma chuckles]

00:51:11.121 --> 00:51:14.124 line:80%
I haven't really made
a great first impression.

00:51:14.792 --> 00:51:16.460 line:80%
-Nice to meet you.
-Hello.

00:51:20.297 --> 00:51:21.674 line:80%
-Let's go.
-[groans]

00:51:22.966 --> 00:51:24.968 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music continuing]

00:51:35.771 --> 00:51:38.857 line:80%
-Isn't that a waste?
-You think so? [chuckles]

00:51:39.483 --> 00:51:43.278 line:80%
But we have to empty it out a few times
to get rid of the impurities.

00:51:43.362 --> 00:51:45.990 line:80%
It makes the flavor
much smoother this way.

00:51:46.907 --> 00:51:48.659 line:80%
It's the same with people.

00:51:48.742 --> 00:51:52.329 line:80%
We have to empty ourselves out
from time to time

00:51:52.413 --> 00:51:55.916 line:80%
to clear our heads and soften our hearts.

00:51:57.459 --> 00:51:59.211 line:80%
[sighs contentedly] The color's nice.

00:51:59.294 --> 00:52:01.547 line:80%
-Try it.
-Thank you.

00:52:03.215 --> 00:52:05.926 line:80%
[exclaims] It's hot. Cool it down a bit.

00:52:07.011 --> 00:52:08.137 line:80%
It's okay, it's not hot.

00:52:08.220 --> 00:52:10.180 line:80%
[grunts, exclaims]

00:52:10.264 --> 00:52:11.598 line:80%
You're right. It's not.

00:52:11.682 --> 00:52:14.059 line:80%
How about some coffee?
I brought Mr. Park's coffee beans.

00:52:14.143 --> 00:52:15.894 line:80%
I'll go and…

00:52:15.978 --> 00:52:18.522 line:80%
I'd prefer tea right now.
[chuckles nervously]

00:52:23.319 --> 00:52:25.988 line:80%
-[gasps] It's delicious.
-Right?

00:52:26.071 --> 00:52:27.072 line:80%
Wow.

00:52:27.740 --> 00:52:30.993 line:80%
The teapot and this cup…

00:52:31.076 --> 00:52:33.329 line:80%
Everything here is so beautiful. [gasps]

00:52:34.204 --> 00:52:37.416 line:80%
They were all made by my grandma.

00:52:38.667 --> 00:52:39.668 line:80%
She's a potter.

00:52:40.753 --> 00:52:43.088 line:80%
-[gasps softly]
-The building outside is my studio.

00:52:43.172 --> 00:52:45.549 line:80%
Would you care to take a look
once you're done?

00:52:45.632 --> 00:52:47.051 line:80%
[stutters]

00:52:49.345 --> 00:52:51.472 line:80%
-[scoffs]
-[exclaims, laughs]

00:52:51.555 --> 00:52:52.765 line:80%
Oh…

00:52:52.848 --> 00:52:55.517 line:80%
Yes… I'd love to take a look. [grimaces]

00:52:55.601 --> 00:52:57.019 line:80%
Hey, Chaewon.

00:52:59.647 --> 00:53:01.106 line:80%
What do you mean, you're sorry?

00:53:05.194 --> 00:53:07.071 line:80%
[sniffs]

00:53:08.906 --> 00:53:09.907 line:80%
What are you doing?

00:53:09.990 --> 00:53:13.952 line:80%
Savoring the only meal I'm having
to get my jawline back.

00:53:14.036 --> 00:53:15.120 line:80%
[keyboard clacking]

00:53:16.121 --> 00:53:17.581 line:80%
-[yells]
-[gasps]

00:53:17.665 --> 00:53:20.000 line:80%
-Oh, my gosh.
-Samples are here!

00:53:23.045 --> 00:53:24.046 line:80%
My sweet potato.

00:53:24.713 --> 00:53:27.883 line:80%
[sighs wearily] I feel like
I swallowed a sock.

00:53:27.966 --> 00:53:30.594 line:80%
What is it? Did something piss you off?

00:53:30.678 --> 00:53:33.097 line:80%
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]
-You know the guy I was seeing?

00:53:33.180 --> 00:53:34.974 line:80%
He cheated.

00:53:35.057 --> 00:53:37.434 line:80%
[Seung-gyu exclaims]
The guy who sent the flowers?

00:53:37.518 --> 00:53:39.061 line:80%
That son of a…

00:53:39.645 --> 00:53:42.064 line:80%
[sighs] I shouldn't swear. With who?

00:53:43.190 --> 00:53:45.693 line:80%
With me. I'm the other woman.

00:53:46.402 --> 00:53:50.864 line:80%
He made a ton of social media accounts
and used them to hit on girls.

00:53:50.948 --> 00:53:54.243 line:80%
And I just heard
he's giving out wedding invitations.

00:53:54.326 --> 00:53:57.579 line:80%
That jerk!
Should I just beat him up? [grunts]

00:53:58.372 --> 00:54:00.958 line:80%
Never mind. Just forget it
and pretend nothing happened.

00:54:01.041 --> 00:54:03.377 line:80%
Why would I just forget about it?

00:54:04.420 --> 00:54:05.421 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:54:05.504 --> 00:54:07.631 line:80%
[exhales] I'm going to crush him.

00:54:12.177 --> 00:54:15.264 line:80%
♪ <i>Happy wedding to you </i>♪

00:54:15.347 --> 00:54:18.642 line:80%
♪ <i>Happy wedding to you </i>♪

00:54:18.726 --> 00:54:21.937 line:80%
♪ <i>Happy wedding, dear Cha Min </i>♪

00:54:22.021 --> 00:54:23.856 line:80%
♪ <i>Happy wedding… </i>♪

00:54:24.690 --> 00:54:26.275 line:80%
Ms. Song.

00:54:26.358 --> 00:54:28.736 line:80%
Were you pleased
with your wedding invitations?

00:54:35.492 --> 00:54:36.827 line:80%
If you found out, just go.

00:54:38.287 --> 00:54:39.747 line:80%
I guess it was you.

00:54:39.830 --> 00:54:42.124 line:80%
I was wondering why
some guy was picking a fight.

00:54:42.207 --> 00:54:44.293 line:80%
Was he your boyfriend?

00:54:44.376 --> 00:54:45.627 line:80%
What are you saying?

00:54:45.711 --> 00:54:47.588 line:80%
How would you meet
a boyfriend I don't have?

00:54:47.671 --> 00:54:48.839 line:80%
Boom!

00:54:48.922 --> 00:54:52.051 line:80%
He threatened me with his car
and threw my phone into a mop bucket.

00:54:52.134 --> 00:54:54.636 line:80%
Geez. I should've broken
both his rear-view mirrors.

00:54:55.512 --> 00:54:58.390 line:80%
Tell that jerk to watch his back at night.

00:54:58.474 --> 00:54:59.558 line:80%
Quit the nonsense.

00:54:59.642 --> 00:55:01.935 line:80%
You should watch your back, day and night.

00:55:02.019 --> 00:55:04.188 line:80%
You should sleep with one eye open.

00:55:04.271 --> 00:55:06.231 line:80%
You never know when I'll crush you.

00:55:06.315 --> 00:55:08.233 line:80%
Forget it. Just go.

00:55:09.777 --> 00:55:10.903 line:80%
I'm not done yet.

00:55:16.992 --> 00:55:18.827 line:80%
-[grunts, whines]
-[♪ upbeat music playing]

00:55:18.952 --> 00:55:20.204 line:80%
My nose…

00:55:20.871 --> 00:55:23.082 line:80%
[whines] I paid a fortune for this.

00:55:23.957 --> 00:55:25.376 line:80%
-Hey!
-What?

00:55:26.543 --> 00:55:27.836 line:80%
You.

00:55:27.920 --> 00:55:29.880 line:80%
You'd better stay out of my sight.

00:55:30.756 --> 00:55:32.299 line:80%
Or I'll kick you somewhere else.

00:55:38.931 --> 00:55:39.932 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:55:42.810 --> 00:55:44.144 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:55:46.271 --> 00:55:47.272 line:80%
[sighs]

00:55:58.701 --> 00:55:59.994 line:80%
Did you go somewhere?

00:56:00.077 --> 00:56:01.453 line:80%
I had a meeting.

00:56:01.537 --> 00:56:02.913 line:80%
Ah…

00:56:02.997 --> 00:56:06.458 line:80%
But is there something wrong?
You seem pretty down.

00:56:07.418 --> 00:56:09.044 line:80%
What? No.

00:56:09.837 --> 00:56:11.088 line:80%
I'm fine.

00:56:11.880 --> 00:56:14.466 line:80%
But why were you riding a cab?

00:56:14.550 --> 00:56:16.427 line:80%
You always drive.

00:56:16.510 --> 00:56:19.388 line:80%
Uh… I had to get it repaired.

00:56:19.471 --> 00:56:21.015 line:80%
Ah. I see.

00:56:22.141 --> 00:56:24.977 line:80%
Head inside.
I'm going to go get some coffee.

00:56:30.107 --> 00:56:32.735 line:80%
I was wondering why
some guy was picking a fight.

00:56:33.861 --> 00:56:35.738 line:80%
I should've broken
both his rear-view mirrors.

00:56:35.821 --> 00:56:38.240 line:80%
"Cha Min." Even his name is nice.

00:56:38.324 --> 00:56:41.327 line:80%
-What do you think, Mr. Yeon?
-I'm not so sure.

00:56:41.410 --> 00:56:44.330 line:80%
-But, Mr. Cha…
-Ms. Kim wants you in her office.

00:56:44.413 --> 00:56:45.706 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:56:45.789 --> 00:56:47.207 line:80%
Are you…

00:56:48.334 --> 00:56:51.420 line:80%
getting it repaired
because of your rear-view mirror?

00:56:51.503 --> 00:56:52.796 line:80%
Yes.

00:56:52.880 --> 00:56:53.881 line:80%
But why…

00:56:53.964 --> 00:56:56.383 line:80%
Are you the one who met Cha Min?

00:56:58.218 --> 00:56:59.219 line:80%
Uh…

00:56:59.303 --> 00:57:02.931 line:80%
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:57:03.015 --> 00:57:05.643 line:80%
Oh. You really have no idea?

00:57:05.726 --> 00:57:09.313 line:80%
Okay, then I'll just go meet him.

00:57:10.272 --> 00:57:13.025 line:80%
Cha Min's number was…

00:57:15.486 --> 00:57:18.405 line:80%
Are you going to say
"Ms. Kim is asking for you" again?

00:57:27.164 --> 00:57:30.042 line:80%
Yes, Ms. Kim. I'll be there straightaway.

00:57:30.125 --> 00:57:31.835 line:80%
You didn't even get a call.

00:57:33.170 --> 00:57:34.588 line:80%
And she already got off work.

00:57:34.672 --> 00:57:36.173 line:80%
[Taeseok] Yes, I'm on my way.

00:57:36.256 --> 00:57:38.384 line:80%
You're holding your phone upside down!

00:57:39.468 --> 00:57:41.178 line:80%
Gosh, what's with him?

00:57:44.723 --> 00:57:45.724 line:80%
[gasps]

00:57:47.017 --> 00:57:49.478 line:80%
Wait. No way…

00:57:51.063 --> 00:57:52.856 line:80%
-[gasps]
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:57:52.940 --> 00:57:55.484 line:80%
It can't be, right?

00:58:01.615 --> 00:58:02.741 line:80%
[Haran] Wow.

00:58:03.742 --> 00:58:04.743 line:80%
Wow.

00:58:05.995 --> 00:58:09.373 line:80%
[gasps] Wow, they're so beautiful.

00:58:09.456 --> 00:58:12.084 line:80%
Take some you like. [chuckles softly]

00:58:12.876 --> 00:58:15.295 line:80%
-[groans]
-They're not even yours. Huh?

00:58:15.963 --> 00:58:18.465 line:80%
-[clears throat]
-[Haran exclaims] What's this drawing?

00:58:18.549 --> 00:58:19.883 line:80%
-Did you draw this, too?
-[Chan] Oh…

00:58:20.634 --> 00:58:22.720 line:80%
Would you like to try
making something here?

00:58:23.470 --> 00:58:24.471 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:58:24.555 --> 00:58:26.265 line:80%
The aprons…

00:58:27.933 --> 00:58:29.935 line:80%
[footsteps thudding]

00:58:33.397 --> 00:58:35.482 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:58:36.317 --> 00:58:37.318 line:80%
[Chan sighs]

00:58:42.990 --> 00:58:43.991 line:80%
I'm done.

00:58:44.491 --> 00:58:46.702 line:80%
-Already?
-[chuckles softly]

00:58:47.494 --> 00:58:49.496 line:80%
-[Haran] Oh, no! Wait.
-[exclaims]

00:58:50.456 --> 00:58:53.459 line:80%
[stutters, sighs in relief]

00:58:53.542 --> 00:58:55.002 line:80%
[chuckles] That was close.

00:58:55.919 --> 00:58:57.755 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:58:59.798 --> 00:59:01.133 line:80%
Let me take this call.

00:59:01.216 --> 00:59:02.259 line:80%
Sure.

00:59:03.677 --> 00:59:04.762 line:80%
[in English] Hello?

00:59:09.350 --> 00:59:10.726 line:80%
[exclaims, gasps]

00:59:10.809 --> 00:59:13.270 line:80%
[exclaims, speaks in Korean]
It's so pretty.

00:59:13.354 --> 00:59:16.065 line:80%
How about becoming my pupil?

00:59:16.148 --> 00:59:18.776 line:80%
-[chuckles]
-[laughs] I mean it.

00:59:18.859 --> 00:59:20.986 line:80%
Leave me your address and phone number.

00:59:21.070 --> 00:59:22.613 line:80%
I'll fire it nicely and send it to you.

00:59:22.696 --> 00:59:24.365 line:80%
[chuckles] Thank you.

00:59:25.240 --> 00:59:27.576 line:80%
I guess Mr. Seonu
inherited his gift from you.

00:59:28.577 --> 00:59:32.331 line:80%
That drawing was his mother's.

00:59:33.791 --> 00:59:35.376 line:80%
My daughter was an artist too.

00:59:35.459 --> 00:59:38.587 line:80%
Ah. So he took after his mother.

00:59:39.088 --> 00:59:43.425 line:80%
He and my daughter would draw
on any piece of paper they could find.

00:59:47.179 --> 00:59:48.639 line:80%
Wait here.

00:59:49.723 --> 00:59:50.724 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:59:50.808 --> 00:59:51.809 line:80%
[gasps]

00:59:52.559 --> 00:59:56.480 line:80%
They're pictures he drew
whenever he came here as a child.

00:59:57.147 --> 00:59:58.983 line:80%
[Haran exclaims, laughs]

00:59:59.066 --> 01:00:01.443 line:80%
He was so excited
when he talked about work.

01:00:02.027 --> 01:00:03.862 line:80%
I guess he really loved drawing.

01:00:05.197 --> 01:00:08.450 line:80%
If his dad hadn't hated it so much,

01:00:08.534 --> 01:00:10.828 line:80%
he would have enjoyed it much more.

01:00:13.539 --> 01:00:14.540 line:80%
Ah. [chuckles]

01:00:15.457 --> 01:00:18.794 line:80%
His father hated him doing art.

01:00:20.170 --> 01:00:22.464 line:80%
But you said his mother was an artist…

01:00:23.966 --> 01:00:28.345 line:80%
Her dream was to go abroad
and study more art.

01:00:29.013 --> 01:00:33.017 line:80%
And Chan's father wanted her
to wait until Chan was older.

01:00:33.100 --> 01:00:34.560 line:80%
-[♪ sentimental music playing]
-Look!

01:00:34.643 --> 01:00:36.520 line:80%
[Chan's dad] Why do we have
to keep arguing over this?

01:00:36.603 --> 01:00:37.813 line:80%
Don't you understand?

01:00:37.896 --> 01:00:40.899 line:20%
Why now? Why do you have
to go abroad to study?

01:00:40.983 --> 01:00:44.611 line:80%
You know it's been my dream
since before we got married. [sighs]

01:00:44.695 --> 01:00:47.948 line:80%
I want to study properly
before it's too late.

01:00:48.032 --> 01:00:49.116 line:80%
Fine. Do it.

01:00:49.199 --> 01:00:53.203 line:80%
You can study here and think about it
again when Chan is older.

01:00:53.287 --> 01:00:55.164 line:80%
You're hardly home anyway!

01:00:56.415 --> 01:00:59.043 line:80%
[sighs] You can stay in your lab
all you want. I'll take Chan--

01:00:59.126 --> 01:01:00.252 line:80%
If you must go,

01:01:01.545 --> 01:01:03.172 line:80%
then leave Chan and go by yourself.

01:01:03.255 --> 01:01:07.051 line:80%
[Chan's grandma]
<i>She still wanted to go so badly.</i>

01:01:07.676 --> 01:01:11.305 line:80%
<i>So I pushed her to follow her dream</i>

01:01:11.388 --> 01:01:14.141 line:80%
<i>and do what she wanted.</i>

01:01:15.017 --> 01:01:18.896 line:80%
<i>She thought she had to settle down quickly</i>
<i>to be with Chan again,</i>

01:01:18.979 --> 01:01:21.857 line:80%
<i>so she pushed herself too hard.</i>

01:01:22.608 --> 01:01:24.276 line:80%
<i>-And she got sick.</i>
-[young Chan sobbing]

01:01:24.360 --> 01:01:27.488 line:80%
<i>Soon after she left the country,</i>

01:01:28.364 --> 01:01:29.823 line:80%
<i>she...</i>

01:01:31.408 --> 01:01:32.409 line:80%
Chan!

01:01:34.078 --> 01:01:35.371 line:80%
Oh, no!

01:01:35.454 --> 01:01:37.039 line:80%
I can't believe what happened…

01:01:37.581 --> 01:01:40.709 line:80%
<i>He said he'd never let Chan paint again.</i>

01:01:41.293 --> 01:01:44.254 line:80%
<i>So he sent him to America.</i>

01:01:44.838 --> 01:01:47.466 line:80%
<i>Chan didn't get to do anything he loved,</i>

01:01:48.092 --> 01:01:51.095 line:80%
<i>and he suffered there.</i>

01:01:51.178 --> 01:01:52.763 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

01:01:56.433 --> 01:01:57.810 line:80%
KSU
KOREA SCIENCE UNIVERSITY

01:01:57.893 --> 01:02:03.732 line:80%
[Chan's grandma] <i>It would've been painful</i>
<i>for Chan's father just to see him paint.</i>

01:02:05.025 --> 01:02:07.236 line:20%
<i>He thinks Chan's mom left to paint...</i>

01:02:07.319 --> 01:02:09.154 line:80%
KOREAN ANIMATORS IN THE GLOBAL SPOTLIGHT

01:02:09.238 --> 01:02:12.032 line:80%
<i>...and died because of it.</i>

01:02:13.826 --> 01:02:15.244 line:80%
[in English] Okay, bye.

01:02:16.078 --> 01:02:19.248 line:80%
[Chan's grandma in Korean] <i>Back then,</i>
<i>my daughter was all I could think about.</i>

01:02:19.331 --> 01:02:23.168 line:80%
<i>But whenever I see Chan,</i>
<i>it breaks my heart.</i>

01:02:23.627 --> 01:02:26.463 line:80%
<i>-</i>[camera clicks]
<i>-If he had his mother,</i>

01:02:26.547 --> 01:02:30.676 line:80%
<i>at least he wouldn't have been hurt</i>
<i>both emotionally and physically.</i>

01:02:31.635 --> 01:02:32.845 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I've also been trapped</i>

01:02:33.762 --> 01:02:36.015 line:80%
<i>in a long winter all by myself.</i>

01:02:40.060 --> 01:02:41.061 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:02:42.521 --> 01:02:43.522 line:80%
[door opens]

01:02:44.898 --> 01:02:45.899 line:80%
Oh?

01:02:46.567 --> 01:02:47.651 line:80%
Where's Ms. Song?

01:02:47.735 --> 01:02:49.236 line:80%
-She's washing her hands.
-Oh.

01:02:51.071 --> 01:02:52.114 line:80%
[Chan sighs]

01:02:52.197 --> 01:02:53.866 line:80%
Is it just one-sided at the moment?

01:02:54.616 --> 01:02:55.617 line:80%
What do you mean?

01:02:57.202 --> 01:02:58.203 line:80%
[Chan sighs]

01:02:58.287 --> 01:03:00.372 line:80%
Gosh, Grandma. It's not like that.

01:03:00.456 --> 01:03:01.957 line:80%
Don't be silly.

01:03:02.541 --> 01:03:03.584 line:80%
I can see it clearly.

01:03:04.418 --> 01:03:06.587 line:80%
You have a crush on Ms. Song, don't you?

01:03:06.670 --> 01:03:08.589 line:80%
It's not like that.

01:03:09.882 --> 01:03:12.051 line:80%
She's someone I shouldn't like.

01:03:12.134 --> 01:03:14.261 line:80%
What do you mean, someone you shouldn't…

01:03:14.845 --> 01:03:17.765 line:80%
[gasps] Hey.
Is she married, by any chance?

01:03:17.848 --> 01:03:19.224 line:80%
No, she's not married.

01:03:19.308 --> 01:03:21.852 line:80%
Then why would you say
you shouldn't like her?

01:03:22.478 --> 01:03:24.563 line:80%
[Haran] Ma'am, can I get a towel?

01:03:24.647 --> 01:03:26.482 line:80%
Sure. Hang on.

01:03:29.401 --> 01:03:30.611 line:80%
[sighs]

01:03:35.616 --> 01:03:38.452 line:80%
[sighs heavily] How could I like her?

01:03:39.953 --> 01:03:41.121 line:80%
That would be selfish.

01:03:42.456 --> 01:03:45.959 line:80%
[Chan's grandma] Visit me again next time.
You can come without that chatterbox.

01:03:46.043 --> 01:03:48.462 line:80%
Sure. I'll come without that chatterbox
next time.

01:03:48.545 --> 01:03:49.922 line:80%
-[Haran chuckles]
-[exclaims]

01:03:50.005 --> 01:03:52.216 line:80%
Don't build your friendship
by badmouthing me.

01:03:52.299 --> 01:03:53.550 line:80%
-[laughs]
-[chuckles]

01:03:54.176 --> 01:03:56.804 line:80%
It was so nice to meet you.

01:03:56.887 --> 01:03:59.014 line:80%
-Take care.
-Stay healthy, ma'am.

01:03:59.098 --> 01:04:01.058 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

01:04:01.141 --> 01:04:03.352 line:80%
Um… Wait.

01:04:05.562 --> 01:04:07.064 line:80%
[Chan's grandma] What's that?

01:04:07.147 --> 01:04:09.483 line:80%
-Pardon me.
-[Chan's grandma gasps]

01:04:10.109 --> 01:04:11.276 line:80%
[Haran] This is really moisturizing.

01:04:11.360 --> 01:04:12.653 line:80%
[both chuckle]

01:04:12.736 --> 01:04:14.238 line:80%
My hands are pretty rough, right?

01:04:14.321 --> 01:04:16.156 line:80%
I'm always touching clay.

01:04:16.240 --> 01:04:17.658 line:80%
Here, use this.

01:04:17.741 --> 01:04:21.787 line:80%
[Chan's grandma exclaims]
I'll get pretty hands thanks to you.

01:04:21.870 --> 01:04:23.205 line:80%
Let's see…

01:04:23.789 --> 01:04:27.251 line:80%
You know, no matter how warm you dress,

01:04:27.334 --> 01:04:29.795 line:80%
you'll catch a cold
if you don't cover your neck.

01:04:29.878 --> 01:04:31.839 line:80%
-I'm okay.
-No, come here.

01:04:31.922 --> 01:04:33.716 line:80%
Here.

01:04:34.633 --> 01:04:36.844 line:80%
Just take it.
You ruined your scarf because of me.

01:04:36.927 --> 01:04:37.970 line:80%
[Chan's grandma] Hmm? Did she?

01:04:38.053 --> 01:04:40.180 line:80%
[gasps] Wow, look.

01:04:40.264 --> 01:04:42.850 line:80%
It looks incredible on a beautiful model.

01:04:42.933 --> 01:04:44.184 line:80%
Nice. This is great.

01:04:44.268 --> 01:04:46.562 line:80%
Thank you. I'll use it well.

01:04:46.645 --> 01:04:48.147 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Grandma.

01:04:48.772 --> 01:04:50.357 line:80%
-[Chan grunts]
-[Chan's grandma chuckles]

01:04:50.441 --> 01:04:52.818 line:80%
I'll come back before I go back to the US.

01:04:52.901 --> 01:04:53.902 line:80%
-[grunts]
-[groans]

01:04:53.986 --> 01:04:56.030 line:80%
You'd better keep your word.

01:04:57.698 --> 01:04:59.325 line:80%
Chan, please. Hmm?

01:05:00.159 --> 01:05:01.827 line:80%
Don't skip your meals. Okay?

01:05:02.328 --> 01:05:03.871 line:80%
Of course. I eat well.

01:05:04.455 --> 01:05:06.290 line:80%
You too, Grandma.

01:05:06.373 --> 01:05:08.250 line:80%
-[Chan's grandma] Don't worry.
-[Chan] Okay.

01:05:09.960 --> 01:05:11.462 line:80%
Bye!

01:05:11.545 --> 01:05:12.796 line:80%
Drive safely!

01:05:16.925 --> 01:05:17.926 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:05:18.010 --> 01:05:19.011 line:80%
[Chan inhales sharply]

01:05:19.094 --> 01:05:22.389 line:80%
Wait. Let's check the windshield wipers
one more time.

01:05:22.973 --> 01:05:24.224 line:80%
-Again?
-Yes.

01:05:28.729 --> 01:05:30.105 line:80%
-Are we good?
-Wait.

01:05:30.189 --> 01:05:31.273 line:80%
[wipers thudding]

01:05:34.193 --> 01:05:37.613 line:80%
Okay. Done. Let's go. [chuckles]

01:05:41.450 --> 01:05:43.410 line:80%
What? Is there something wrong again?

01:05:44.078 --> 01:05:45.871 line:80%
Yes, there is.

01:05:46.497 --> 01:05:47.498 line:80%
Something strange.

01:05:48.832 --> 01:05:50.292 line:80%
What's strange?

01:05:53.253 --> 01:05:56.674 line:80%
Why am I someone you shouldn't like?

01:05:58.425 --> 01:05:59.551 line:80%
What?

01:06:01.095 --> 01:06:02.971 line:80%
Why shouldn't you like me?

01:06:03.555 --> 01:06:05.557 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

01:06:06.100 --> 01:06:08.602 line:80%
[Chan's grandma]
You have a crush on Ms. Song, don't you?

01:06:09.228 --> 01:06:10.479 line:80%
It's not like that.

01:06:11.063 --> 01:06:12.648 line:80%
She's someone I shouldn't like.

01:06:13.899 --> 01:06:15.818 line:80%
[Chan's grandma]
What do you mean, someone you shouldn't…

01:06:16.944 --> 01:06:19.780 line:80%
[gasps] Hey.
Is she married, by any chance?

01:06:19.863 --> 01:06:21.365 line:80%
[Chan] No, she's not married.

01:06:21.448 --> 01:06:23.993 line:80%
[Chan's grandma] Then why would you say
you shouldn't like her?

01:06:24.076 --> 01:06:26.245 line:80%
Ma'am, can I get a towel?

01:06:26.328 --> 01:06:28.664 line:80%
[Chan's grandma] Sure. Hang on.

01:06:28.747 --> 01:06:31.041 line:80%
I'm sorry, but I overheard.

01:06:31.667 --> 01:06:33.919 line:80%
I really couldn't understand, though.

01:06:34.628 --> 01:06:36.880 line:80%
You weren't saying
that you didn't like me.

01:06:36.964 --> 01:06:40.968 line:80%
You said you shouldn't like me.
[chuckles] That sounds weird.

01:06:42.177 --> 01:06:43.178 line:80%
[sighs]

01:06:46.890 --> 01:06:48.350 line:80%
It's not like I'm married.

01:06:48.434 --> 01:06:51.603 line:80%
There's nothing between us
that would make it wrong.

01:06:52.438 --> 01:06:54.023 line:80%
What did you mean by that?

01:06:58.610 --> 01:07:02.698 line:80%
Oh… I'm not trying to argue or anything.
I'm just genuinely curious.

01:07:02.781 --> 01:07:04.450 line:80%
Then is it okay if I like you?

01:07:04.533 --> 01:07:06.535 line:80%
[wipers thudding]

01:07:08.162 --> 01:07:09.163 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:07:17.296 --> 01:07:18.547 line:80%
[stutters]

01:07:18.630 --> 01:07:19.631 line:80%
[sighs]

01:07:22.426 --> 01:07:24.511 line:80%
[wiper thuds echoing]

01:07:27.014 --> 01:07:29.475 line:80%
[heartbeats echoing]

01:07:32.394 --> 01:07:34.396 line:80%
[♪ romantic song playing]

01:07:46.575 --> 01:07:48.494 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:08:13.018 --> 01:08:16.397 line:20%
[Haran] <i>The person</i>
<i>who gave me the pen died.</i>

01:08:16.480 --> 01:08:20.234 line:20%
[Chan] <i>What else was there</i>
<i>apart from the explosion?</i>

01:08:20.317 --> 01:08:22.111 line:20%
[Haran] <i>Honestly, I am curious.</i>

01:08:22.194 --> 01:08:25.698 line:20%
<i>You're not telling me everything.</i>

01:08:26.699 --> 01:08:31.203 line:20%
[Chan] <i>The past might not be</i>
<i>as nice as you remember.</i>

01:08:31.829 --> 01:08:34.540 line:20%
<i>I'll explain everything</i>
<i>if you guess it right.</i>

01:08:34.623 --> 01:08:38.335 line:20%
<i>I feel like telling you everything today.</i>

01:08:39.211 --> 01:08:40.254 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Odd.</i>

01:08:41.171 --> 01:08:42.297 line:80%
Odd.

01:08:45.384 --> 01:08:46.385 line:80%
[♪ song fades]

01:08:46.468 --> 01:08:48.470 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

01:08:54.351 --> 01:08:55.352 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:08:55.436 --> 01:08:56.437 line:80%
Translated by Juyoung Park